    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# AEPG: Australian Generate a PIN Pad Proof of End Point (AS2805)\n\nFuente: [AEPG: Australian Generate a PIN Pad Proof of End Point (AS2805)](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/pins/generate/aepg-australian-generate-a-pin-pad-proof-of-end-point-as2805)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:00:19.057Z\n\n---\n\nThis command generates a PIN pad proof of end point for Australian standards (AS2805).\n\n> **Warning:** Disabled in PCI HSM Mode Pending PCI Approval\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| Australian Command Set | Enables payments-related commands per the AS2805 messaging standard, as defined by AusPayNet. |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `AEPG` |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-major-key\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - Major key\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: MFK<br>`6`: PMK (default)<br>`7`: FTK (if PKCS #11 is available) |\n\n<a id=\"ak-dek\"></a>\n\n### AK - DEK\n\nUsed for decrypting (recovering) PPASN in token **GN**.\n\nThis field supports the following formats:\n\n- Cryptogram encrypted under modifier 2 of the major key\n- TR-31 key block  \n\n  - **Key Usage**: D0\n  - **Algorithm**: T, D\n  - **Mode of Use**: B, D\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16<br>32<br>48 | Hexadecimal | **Cryptogram**<br>0 - 9, A - F |\n| Variable | ASCII | **Key block**<br>A - Z, a - z, 0 - 9 except ; [ ] |\n\n<a id=\"aj-kek\"></a>\n\n### AJ - KEK\n\nUsed for generating (encrypting) the POEP.\n\nThis field supports the following formats:\n\n- Cryptogram encrypted under modifier 0 of the major key\n- TR-31 key block  \n\n  - **Key Usage**: K0\n  - **Algorithm**: T, D\n  - **Mode of Use**: B, E\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16<br>32<br>48 | Hexadecimal | **Cryptogram**<br>0 - 9, A - F |\n| Variable | ASCII | **Key block**<br>A - Z, a - z, 0 - 9 except ; [ ] |\n\n<a id=\"gn-pin-pad-acquirer-secret-number-ppsan\"></a>\n\n### GN - PIN pad acquirer secret number (PPSAN)\n\nEncrypted under DEK (**AK**token)\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16 | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `AEPG` |\n\n<a id=\"bo-pin-pad-proof-of-end-point-poep\"></a>\n\n### BO - PIN pad proof of end point (POEP)\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 8 | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"command-example\"></a>\n\n## Command example\n\n```\nRequest: [AOAEPG;GN8AB29340CD8D98A2;AKB0080D0TB00E00004FC3B6C67FBC3572D3E7D5053E41B84258EC0D31E4C3D8ABE8E0DE89B004E98B;FS1;AJB0080K0TB00E00006A35171735DC596055234009C87D94B1B3098654DB5C2AB49F6A5F60685579FA;]\n\nResponse: [AOAEPG;BODC93A1DE;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"changelog\"></a>\n\n## Changelog\n\n2024-07-03\n\n- Added **FW-12532** | New Excrypt command\n",
      "en": "# AEPG: Australian Generate a PIN Pad Proof of End Point (AS2805)\n\nFuente: [AEPG: Australian Generate a PIN Pad Proof of End Point (AS2805)](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/pins/generate/aepg-australian-generate-a-pin-pad-proof-of-end-point-as2805)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:00:19.057Z\n\n---\n\nThis command generates a PIN pad proof of end point for Australian standards (AS2805).\n\n> **Warning:** Disabled in PCI HSM Mode Pending PCI Approval\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| Australian Command Set | Enables payments-related commands per the AS2805 messaging standard, as defined by AusPayNet. |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `AEPG` |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-major-key\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - Major key\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: MFK<br>`6`: PMK (default)<br>`7`: FTK (if PKCS #11 is available) |\n\n<a id=\"ak-dek\"></a>\n\n### AK - DEK\n\nUsed for decrypting (recovering) PPASN in token **GN**.\n\nThis field supports the following formats:\n\n- Cryptogram encrypted under modifier 2 of the major key\n- TR-31 key block  \n\n  - **Key Usage**: D0\n  - **Algorithm**: T, D\n  - **Mode of Use**: B, D\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16<br>32<br>48 | Hexadecimal | **Cryptogram**<br>0 - 9, A - F |\n| Variable | ASCII | **Key block**<br>A - Z, a - z, 0 - 9 except ; [ ] |\n\n<a id=\"aj-kek\"></a>\n\n### AJ - KEK\n\nUsed for generating (encrypting) the POEP.\n\nThis field supports the following formats:\n\n- Cryptogram encrypted under modifier 0 of the major key\n- TR-31 key block  \n\n  - **Key Usage**: K0\n  - **Algorithm**: T, D\n  - **Mode of Use**: B, E\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16<br>32<br>48 | Hexadecimal | **Cryptogram**<br>0 - 9, A - F |\n| Variable | ASCII | **Key block**<br>A - Z, a - z, 0 - 9 except ; [ ] |\n\n<a id=\"gn-pin-pad-acquirer-secret-number-ppsan\"></a>\n\n### GN - PIN pad acquirer secret number (PPSAN)\n\nEncrypted under DEK (**AK**token)\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16 | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `AEPG` |\n\n<a id=\"bo-pin-pad-proof-of-end-point-poep\"></a>\n\n### BO - PIN pad proof of end point (POEP)\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 8 | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"command-example\"></a>\n\n## Command example\n\n```\nRequest: [AOAEPG;GN8AB29340CD8D98A2;AKB0080D0TB00E00004FC3B6C67FBC3572D3E7D5053E41B84258EC0D31E4C3D8ABE8E0DE89B004E98B;FS1;AJB0080K0TB00E00006A35171735DC596055234009C87D94B1B3098654DB5C2AB49F6A5F60685579FA;]\n\nResponse: [AOAEPG;BODC93A1DE;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"changelog\"></a>\n\n## Changelog\n\n2024-07-03\n\n- Added **FW-12532** | New Excrypt command\n"
    }
