    "name": {
      "es": "AKVR: Australian Generate a KEKr Validation Response (AS2805)",
      "en": "AKVR: Australian Generate a KEKr Validation Response (AS2805)"
    },
    "summary": {
      "es": "This command generates a Key Encryption Key - Receive (KEKr) validation response for Australian standards (AS2805).\n\nAKVR is the receiver half of the AS2805 KEK validation exchange. The sender runs [AKVS](akvs-australian-generate-a-keks-validation-request-as2805.md), keeps its own `AR` value, and transmits `BO`. The receiver runs AKVR with that `BO` and returns the `AR` value in this response. The sender then compares the two values: a match confirms both sides hold the same KEK. The KRr in `AR` is the validation response for that comparison only. It is not an agreed working key, and neither side uses it as one afterward.\n\n> **Warning:** Disabled in PCI HSM Mode Pending PCI Approval",
      "en": "This command generates a Key Encryption Key - Receive (KEKr) validation response for Australian standards (AS2805).\n\nAKVR is the receiver half of the AS2805 KEK validation exchange. The sender runs [AKVS](akvs-australian-generate-a-keks-validation-request-as2805.md), keeps its own `AR` value, and transmits `BO`. The receiver runs AKVR with that `BO` and returns the `AR` value in this response. The sender then compares the two values: a match confirms both sides hold the same KEK. The KRr in `AR` is the validation response for that comparison only. It is not an agreed working key, and neither side uses it as one afterward.\n\n> **Warning:** Disabled in PCI HSM Mode Pending PCI Approval"
    },
