      "es": "This command generates a Key Encryption Key - Send (KEKs) validation request for Australian standards (AS2805).\n\nThe sender runs AKVS, keeps the `AR` value locally, and transmits `BO` to the receiver. The receiver runs [AKVR](akvr-australian-generate-a-kekr-validation-response-as2805.md) with that `BO` and returns the `AR` value it derives independently. The sender then compares the returned value with the `AR` it retained: a match confirms both sides hold the same KEK. The KRr in `AR` is the validation response for that comparison only. It is not an agreed working key, and neither side uses it as one afterward.\n\n> **Warning:** Disabled in PCI HSM Mode Pending PCI Approval\n\n> **Note:** On the 7.6 release line, use firmware version 7.6.1.35 or later for AS2805 KEK validation. Earlier builds read request token **CT** as a key type instead of a nonce length. See the **CT** token section and the changelog below.",
