      "es": "This command starts nonce-based PKI authentication, asking you to send a certificate to the HSM that can be verified with the CA certificate uploaded by using the **IDEN** command. This process uses the common name of the certificate to look up the administrator to log in. It then issues a nonce and expects it to be signed by the private key associated with the admin certificate.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Requirements**\n\n- Excrypt command **APKK** is required to complete authentication.\n- CA certificate uploaded to identity.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- See Excrypt command **APKK** for signature requirements.",
