    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# APKJ: Starts Nonce-based PKI Authentication\n\nFuente: [APKJ: Starts Nonce-based PKI Authentication](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/system/authentication/apkj-starts-nonce-based-pki-authentication)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:00:52.631Z\n\n---\n\nThis command starts nonce-based PKI authentication, asking you to send a certificate to the HSM that can be verified with the CA certificate uploaded by using the **IDEN** command. This process uses the common name of the certificate to look up the administrator to log in. It then issues a nonce and expects it to be signed by the private key associated with the admin certificate.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Requirements**\n\n- Excrypt command **APKK** is required to complete authentication.\n- CA certificate uploaded to identity.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- See Excrypt command **APKK** for signature requirements.\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `CE` | User certificate | Hexadecimal | 2-4096 | Yes |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `DA` | Username | ASCII | 4-16 |\n| `BO` | Challenge to sign | Hexadecimal | 64 |\n| `CH` | Continuation ID | Numeric | 1-24 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `APKJ` |\n\n<a id=\"ce-user-certificate\"></a>\n\n### CE - User certificate\n\nCommon name = Username\n\nMust be at least RSA 2048/ECC 224 and equal to or less than the strength of the registered identity CA.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2-4096 | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `APKJ` |\n\n<a id=\"da-username\"></a>\n\n### DA - Username\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4-16 | ASCII | A - Z, a - z, 0 - 9 except ; [ ] |\n\n<a id=\"bo-challenge-to-sign\"></a>\n\n### BO - Challenge to sign\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 64 | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"ch-continuation-id\"></a>\n\n### CH - Continuation ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-24 | Numeric | 0 - 9 |\n\n<a id=\"command-example\"></a>\n\n### Command example\n\n```\nRequest: [AOAPKJ;;]\n\nResponse: [AOAPKJ;DAAdmin3;BOF0AC74C5E4C56D3D8EAF512DAF67EE40ADAE15E99CBEA140849E19A66369A5AF;CH1246841382;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"changelog\"></a>\n\n## Changelog\n\n2026-05-27\n\n- Fixed **FW-18884** | Resolved an issue that immediately logged the user out of a successfully authenticated session while in PCI-HSM mode.\n\n2024-07-03\n\n- Added **FW-13926** | Inactive PKI authorization sessions are now cleared after 5 minutes.\n- Added **FW-13812** | PKI authentication is now allowed to be shared across multiple connections.\n- Added **FW-13775** | In PCI HSM mode, the identity CA must have a minimum size of RSA 2048 or ECC 224.\n- Added **FW-12767** | Enabled in PCI HSM mode.\n",
      "en": "# APKJ: Starts Nonce-based PKI Authentication\n\nFuente: [APKJ: Starts Nonce-based PKI Authentication](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/system/authentication/apkj-starts-nonce-based-pki-authentication)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:00:52.631Z\n\n---\n\nThis command starts nonce-based PKI authentication, asking you to send a certificate to the HSM that can be verified with the CA certificate uploaded by using the **IDEN** command. This process uses the common name of the certificate to look up the administrator to log in. It then issues a nonce and expects it to be signed by the private key associated with the admin certificate.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Requirements**\n\n- Excrypt command **APKK** is required to complete authentication.\n- CA certificate uploaded to identity.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- See Excrypt command **APKK** for signature requirements.\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `CE` | User certificate | Hexadecimal | 2-4096 | Yes |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `DA` | Username | ASCII | 4-16 |\n| `BO` | Challenge to sign | Hexadecimal | 64 |\n| `CH` | Continuation ID | Numeric | 1-24 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `APKJ` |\n\n<a id=\"ce-user-certificate\"></a>\n\n### CE - User certificate\n\nCommon name = Username\n\nMust be at least RSA 2048/ECC 224 and equal to or less than the strength of the registered identity CA.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2-4096 | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `APKJ` |\n\n<a id=\"da-username\"></a>\n\n### DA - Username\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4-16 | ASCII | A - Z, a - z, 0 - 9 except ; [ ] |\n\n<a id=\"bo-challenge-to-sign\"></a>\n\n### BO - Challenge to sign\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 64 | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"ch-continuation-id\"></a>\n\n### CH - Continuation ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-24 | Numeric | 0 - 9 |\n\n<a id=\"command-example\"></a>\n\n### Command example\n\n```\nRequest: [AOAPKJ;;]\n\nResponse: [AOAPKJ;DAAdmin3;BOF0AC74C5E4C56D3D8EAF512DAF67EE40ADAE15E99CBEA140849E19A66369A5AF;CH1246841382;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"changelog\"></a>\n\n## Changelog\n\n2026-05-27\n\n- Fixed **FW-18884** | Resolved an issue that immediately logged the user out of a successfully authenticated session while in PCI-HSM mode.\n\n2024-07-03\n\n- Added **FW-13926** | Inactive PKI authorization sessions are now cleared after 5 minutes.\n- Added **FW-13812** | PKI authentication is now allowed to be shared across multiple connections.\n- Added **FW-13775** | In PCI HSM mode, the identity CA must have a minimum size of RSA 2048 or ECC 224.\n- Added **FW-12767** | Enabled in PCI HSM mode.\n"
    }
