    "id": "futurex-asgc-req",
    "code": "ASGC",
    "direction": "request",
    "pairedCode": "ASGC",
    "name": {
      "es": "ASGC: Generate a PKI Signed Certificate",
      "en": "ASGC: Generate a PKI Signed Certificate"
    },
    "summary": {
      "es": "This command generates a PKI-signed certificate. If the parent private key has the anonymous signing usage flag, this command should allow sending in clear public keys into the public key token **RD**.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in FIPS mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This command supports Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC) keys. You must enable the PQC license to use these keys.\n- PQC issuer/subject certificate generation is currently disabled in PCI HSM mode pending PCI approval.\n- SHA3 and SHAKE hashing algorithms can be used in FIPS mode in FW version 7.6.1.10 and later.",
      "en": "This command generates a PKI-signed certificate. If the parent private key has the anonymous signing usage flag, this command should allow sending in clear public keys into the public key token **RD**.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in FIPS mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This command supports Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC) keys. You must enable the PQC license to use these keys.\n- PQC issuer/subject certificate generation is currently disabled in PCI HSM mode pending PCI approval.\n- SHA3 and SHAKE hashing algorithms can be used in FIPS mode in FW version 7.6.1.10 and later."
    },
    "description": {
      "es": "This command generates a PKI-signed certificate. If the parent private key has the anonymous signing usage flag, this command should allow sending in clear public keys into the public key token **RD**.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in FIPS mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This command supports Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC) keys. You must enable the PQC license to use these keys.\n- PQC issuer/subject certificate generation is currently disabled in PCI HSM mode pending PCI approval.\n- SHA3 and SHAKE hashing algorithms can be used in FIPS mode in FW version 7.6.1.10 and later.",
      "en": "This command generates a PKI-signed certificate. If the parent private key has the anonymous signing usage flag, this command should allow sending in clear public keys into the public key token **RD**.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in FIPS mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This command supports Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC) keys. You must enable the PQC license to use these keys.\n- PQC issuer/subject certificate generation is currently disabled in PCI HSM mode pending PCI approval.\n- SHA3 and SHAKE hashing algorithms can be used in FIPS mode in FW version 7.6.1.10 and later."
    },
