      "en": "This command verifies a PKCS #7 or X.509 certificate and returns the trusted public key encrypted under a specified major key.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This command defaults to TR-31 type B for DES KEKs and TR-31 type D for AES KEKs.\n- You can enable **AVPC/RVPC Ignore Certificate Expiration**under **Function Settings** on the Web Portal to ignore the validity date check.\n- This command supports Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC) keys. You must enable the PQC license to use these keys.\n- If using PQC keys, it is recommended to change the **Max Request Message Length** on the HSM to at least 16k bytes.\n- Importing a PQC key in TPK format from a PQC certificate is currently disabled in PCI HSM mode pending PCI approval."
