    "id": "futurex-cdtr-req",
    "code": "CDTR",
    "direction": "request",
    "pairedCode": "CDTR",
    "name": {
      "es": "CDTR: Convert Base64 and Hexadecimal Data",
      "en": "CDTR: Convert Base64 and Hexadecimal Data"
    },
    "summary": {
      "es": "This command converts a provided value between Base64 and hexadecimal.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This command can convert values up to and including 4096 in hexadecimal, 2800 in base64.\n- When converting from hexadecimal to base64 the output should always be a multiple of four characters; if there’s not enough input data for that many, it is padded with equal (=) signs.\n- When converting from base64 to hexadecimal the result can be any even number of characters. When sending hex data, make sure you always send an even number of characters, as each byte is two characters in hex.",
      "en": "This command converts a provided value between Base64 and hexadecimal.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This command can convert values up to and including 4096 in hexadecimal, 2800 in base64.\n- When converting from hexadecimal to base64 the output should always be a multiple of four characters; if there’s not enough input data for that many, it is padded with equal (=) signs.\n- When converting from base64 to hexadecimal the result can be any even number of characters. When sending hex data, make sure you always send an even number of characters, as each byte is two characters in hex."
    },
    "description": {
      "es": "This command converts a provided value between Base64 and hexadecimal.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This command can convert values up to and including 4096 in hexadecimal, 2800 in base64.\n- When converting from hexadecimal to base64 the output should always be a multiple of four characters; if there’s not enough input data for that many, it is padded with equal (=) signs.\n- When converting from base64 to hexadecimal the result can be any even number of characters. When sending hex data, make sure you always send an even number of characters, as each byte is two characters in hex.",
      "en": "This command converts a provided value between Base64 and hexadecimal.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This command can convert values up to and including 4096 in hexadecimal, 2800 in base64.\n- When converting from hexadecimal to base64 the output should always be a multiple of four characters; if there’s not enough input data for that many, it is padded with equal (=) signs.\n- When converting from base64 to hexadecimal the result can be any even number of characters. When sending hex data, make sure you always send an even number of characters, as each byte is two characters in hex."
    },
