    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# CPTY: Check Parity of Working Buffer\n\nFuente: [CPTY: Check Parity of Working Buffer](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/validate/cpty-check-parity-of-working-buffer)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:01:13.096Z\n\n---\n\nThis command modifies the parity of the working buffer.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- When a key is being loaded as separate components, it is stored in the working buffer. This command either forces an odd parity or checks to determine if an odd parity is already enforced or not.\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Keys:Import Components | Create keys from one or more clear components. | Mgmt | 2/1 |\n| Major Keys:Load | Load major keys (components, smart cards). | Mgmt | 2 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `CPTY` |\n\n<a id=\"optional-ak-force-key-to-have-odd-parity\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) AK - Force key to have odd parity\n\nIf not sent, the command returns the current parity status of the key in token **BB**.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 3 | Alphabetic | `ODD` |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id-2\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `CPTY` |\n\n<a id=\"ak-force-key-to-have-odd-parity\"></a>\n\n### AK - Force key to have odd parity\n\nNot returned if request token **AK** is not sent.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 3 | Alphabetic | `ODD` |\n\n<a id=\"bb-display-parity\"></a>\n\n### BB - Display parity\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2-4 | Alphabetic | `OK`: Odd parity set for working buffer<br>`ODD`: Working buffer already has odd parity<br>`NONE`: Working buffer does not have odd parity |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"odd-parity-set-for-working-buffer\"></a>\n\n## Odd parity set for working buffer\n\n```\nRequest: [AOCPTY;AKODD;]\n\nResponse: [AOCPTY;AKODD;BBOK;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"working-buffer-already-has-odd-parity\"></a>\n\n## Working buffer already has odd parity\n\n```\nRequest: [AOCPTY;]\n\nResponse: [AOCPTY;BBODD;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"working-buffer-does-not-have-odd-parity\"></a>\n\n## Working buffer does not have odd parity\n\n```\nRequest: [AOCPTY;]\n\nResponse: [AOCPTY;BBNONE;]\n```\n",
      "en": "# CPTY: Check Parity of Working Buffer\n\nFuente: [CPTY: Check Parity of Working Buffer](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/validate/cpty-check-parity-of-working-buffer)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:01:13.096Z\n\n---\n\nThis command modifies the parity of the working buffer.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- When a key is being loaded as separate components, it is stored in the working buffer. This command either forces an odd parity or checks to determine if an odd parity is already enforced or not.\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Keys:Import Components | Create keys from one or more clear components. | Mgmt | 2/1 |\n| Major Keys:Load | Load major keys (components, smart cards). | Mgmt | 2 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `CPTY` |\n\n<a id=\"optional-ak-force-key-to-have-odd-parity\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) AK - Force key to have odd parity\n\nIf not sent, the command returns the current parity status of the key in token **BB**.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 3 | Alphabetic | `ODD` |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id-2\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `CPTY` |\n\n<a id=\"ak-force-key-to-have-odd-parity\"></a>\n\n### AK - Force key to have odd parity\n\nNot returned if request token **AK** is not sent.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 3 | Alphabetic | `ODD` |\n\n<a id=\"bb-display-parity\"></a>\n\n### BB - Display parity\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2-4 | Alphabetic | `OK`: Odd parity set for working buffer<br>`ODD`: Working buffer already has odd parity<br>`NONE`: Working buffer does not have odd parity |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"odd-parity-set-for-working-buffer\"></a>\n\n## Odd parity set for working buffer\n\n```\nRequest: [AOCPTY;AKODD;]\n\nResponse: [AOCPTY;AKODD;BBOK;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"working-buffer-already-has-odd-parity\"></a>\n\n## Working buffer already has odd parity\n\n```\nRequest: [AOCPTY;]\n\nResponse: [AOCPTY;BBODD;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"working-buffer-does-not-have-odd-parity\"></a>\n\n## Working buffer does not have odd parity\n\n```\nRequest: [AOCPTY;]\n\nResponse: [AOCPTY;BBNONE;]\n```\n"
    }
