    "name": {
      "es": "CWKS: Create Working Key for Storage",
      "en": "CWKS: Create Working Key for Storage"
    },
    "summary": {
      "es": "This command creates a single- or double-length working key from components entered into the working buffer, encrypts it under a specified modifier of the MFK, and returns a cryptogram or key block in the response.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The cryptogram can generate international key blocks if done over the admin port with the Excrypt UI feature enabled.\n- Before you can execute this command, you must load key components into the working buffer by executing the **LKEY: Load Clear Key Component** command as many times as is required to build a key. This command then creates a cryptogram or key block based on the contents of the working buffer encrypted under the MFK with the modifier or key block header specified in token **AS**.\n- The working buffer is cleared upon command execution.",
      "en": "This command creates a single- or double-length working key from components entered into the working buffer, encrypts it under a specified modifier of the MFK, and returns a cryptogram or key block in the response.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The cryptogram can generate international key blocks if done over the admin port with the Excrypt UI feature enabled.\n- Before you can execute this command, you must load key components into the working buffer by executing the **LKEY: Load Clear Key Component** command as many times as is required to build a key. This command then creates a cryptogram or key block based on the contents of the working buffer encrypted under the MFK with the modifier or key block header specified in token **AS**.\n- The working buffer is cleared upon command execution."
    },
    "description": {
      "es": "This command creates a single- or double-length working key from components entered into the working buffer, encrypts it under a specified modifier of the MFK, and returns a cryptogram or key block in the response.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The cryptogram can generate international key blocks if done over the admin port with the Excrypt UI feature enabled.\n- Before you can execute this command, you must load key components into the working buffer by executing the **LKEY: Load Clear Key Component** command as many times as is required to build a key. This command then creates a cryptogram or key block based on the contents of the working buffer encrypted under the MFK with the modifier or key block header specified in token **AS**.\n- The working buffer is cleared upon command execution.",
      "en": "This command creates a single- or double-length working key from components entered into the working buffer, encrypts it under a specified modifier of the MFK, and returns a cryptogram or key block in the response.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The cryptogram can generate international key blocks if done over the admin port with the Excrypt UI feature enabled.\n- Before you can execute this command, you must load key components into the working buffer by executing the **LKEY: Load Clear Key Component** command as many times as is required to build a key. This command then creates a cryptogram or key block based on the contents of the working buffer encrypted under the MFK with the modifier or key block header specified in token **AS**.\n- The working buffer is cleared upon command execution."
    },
