    "summary": {
      "es": "This command decrypts cardholder data (PAN) that has been encrypted using Triple DES under a key derived from a DUKPT BDK.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- Because this command in PIN variant mode returns clear cardholder data, it is not considered safe, and we require you to sign a waiver to enable this mode. We strongly recommend that you use PIN variant mode in an isolated and segregated HSM environment with appropriate controls in place.\n- The PIN variant is only available with the CPIN feature enabled and only allowed in PCI mode for issuing environments.\n- For more information about DUKPT, see ANSI X9.24, Part 1 - Annex A.",
      "en": "This command decrypts cardholder data (PAN) that has been encrypted using Triple DES under a key derived from a DUKPT BDK.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- Because this command in PIN variant mode returns clear cardholder data, it is not considered safe, and we require you to sign a waiver to enable this mode. We strongly recommend that you use PIN variant mode in an isolated and segregated HSM environment with appropriate controls in place.\n- The PIN variant is only available with the CPIN feature enabled and only allowed in PCI mode for issuing environments.\n- For more information about DUKPT, see ANSI X9.24, Part 1 - Annex A."
    },
