      "en": "The DCMT command saves or deletes the default RFD (Reset to Factory Defaults) profile configuration on an HSM. Use the `OP` token to specify whether to save or delete, and the `MD` token to query whether the operation is allowed before committing. This is useful for preserving a known-good configuration that can be restored via the RFDC command.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The HSM must be signed and must not be running in Docker or as a virtual HSM.\n- The HSM’s RFD firmware and active firmware must be the same version to save a configuration.\n- Use `MD0` (query mode) first to check whether the operation is allowed before committing with `MD1`."
