    "summary": {
      "es": "The DIAG command returns system diagnostics from the HSM. The response includes CPU utilization, memory usage, network throughput, connection counts, uptime, and hardware-specific values such as temperature, battery voltage, fan status, and power supply status. Use this command to monitor HSM health or integrate with external monitoring systems.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- Some values are not real-time; they are recalculated every 4-5 seconds.\n- Hardware-specific tokens (BS, CA, DA, EA, PG, PS) are only returned on applicable platforms (GSP, GSPv2, EXP1000).",
      "en": "The DIAG command returns system diagnostics from the HSM. The response includes CPU utilization, memory usage, network throughput, connection counts, uptime, and hardware-specific values such as temperature, battery voltage, fan status, and power supply status. Use this command to monitor HSM health or integrate with external monitoring systems.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- Some values are not real-time; they are recalculated every 4-5 seconds.\n- Hardware-specific tokens (BS, CA, DA, EA, PG, PS) are only returned on applicable platforms (GSP, GSPv2, EXP1000)."
    },
