      "en": "This command derives a key function by using the NIST SP 800-108 key derivation function in counter mode (5.1). For further reference, see the NIST Special Publication 800-108: Recommendation for Key Derivation Using Pseudorandom Functions and Key Derivation using Pseudorandom Functions (SP 800-108) Validation System (KBKDFVS).\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The following assumptions were applied from NIST SP800-108 into the current implementation of this command: \n\n  - R (length of the binary representation of the counter) equals `8`.\n  - Context and footer length of fixed content data are optional.\n  - DES1-derived keys are not allowed because they are not in the KBKDFVS."
