    "summary": {
      "es": "This command deletes a specified RSA key in the key table.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- While the API recognizes PKI storage to be slots 0-99, the Excrypt Manager loads keys into slots 1-100. Therefore, for tokens that support PKI storage table indexing, the key slot in which the key is loaded by using Excrypt Manager is off by one. For example, a key loaded into slot **1** on the Excrypt Manager is referenced in the API as slot **0**.",
      "en": "This command deletes a specified RSA key in the key table.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- While the API recognizes PKI storage to be slots 0-99, the Excrypt Manager loads keys into slots 1-100. Therefore, for tokens that support PKI storage table indexing, the key slot in which the key is loaded by using Excrypt Manager is off by one. For example, a key loaded into slot **1** on the Excrypt Manager is referenced in the API as slot **0**."
    },
    "description": {
      "es": "This command deletes a specified RSA key in the key table.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- While the API recognizes PKI storage to be slots 0-99, the Excrypt Manager loads keys into slots 1-100. Therefore, for tokens that support PKI storage table indexing, the key slot in which the key is loaded by using Excrypt Manager is off by one. For example, a key loaded into slot **1** on the Excrypt Manager is referenced in the API as slot **0**.",
      "en": "This command deletes a specified RSA key in the key table.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- While the API recognizes PKI storage to be slots 0-99, the Excrypt Manager loads keys into slots 1-100. Therefore, for tokens that support PKI storage table indexing, the key slot in which the key is loaded by using Excrypt Manager is off by one. For example, a key loaded into slot **1** on the Excrypt Manager is referenced in the API as slot **0**."
    },
