    "source": "Futurex Excrypt Command Reference Manual v7.6.1 (DRSA)",
    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# DRSA: Delete RSA Key from Key Table\n\nFuente: [DRSA: Delete RSA Key from Key Table](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/key_tables/drsa-delete-rsa-key-from-key-table)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:02:18.213Z\n\n---\n\nThis command deletes a specified RSA key in the key table.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- While the API recognizes PKI storage to be slots 0-99, the Excrypt Manager loads keys into slots 1-100. Therefore, for tokens that support PKI storage table indexing, the key slot in which the key is loaded by using Excrypt Manager is off by one. For example, a key loaded into slot **1** on the Excrypt Manager is referenced in the API as slot **0**.\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| RSA | Enables commands requiring RSA functionality. |\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Keys | View key and table information | Mgmt | 0 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `RD` | Index of the RSA key that is being deleted | Numeric | 1-2 | Yes |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `BQ` | Number of available RSA key slots | Numeric | 2 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `DRSA` |\n\n<a id=\"rd-index-of-the-rsa-key-that-is-being-deleted\"></a>\n\n### RD - Index of the RSA key that is being deleted\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-2 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `DRSA` |\n\n<a id=\"bq-number-of-available-rsa-key-slots\"></a>\n\n### BQ - Number of available RSA key slots\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"command-example\"></a>\n\n## Command example\n\n```\nRequest: [AODRSA;RD20;]\n\nResponse: [AODRSA;BQ80;]\n```\n",
      "en": "# DRSA: Delete RSA Key from Key Table\n\nFuente: [DRSA: Delete RSA Key from Key Table](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/key_tables/drsa-delete-rsa-key-from-key-table)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:02:18.213Z\n\n---\n\nThis command deletes a specified RSA key in the key table.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- While the API recognizes PKI storage to be slots 0-99, the Excrypt Manager loads keys into slots 1-100. Therefore, for tokens that support PKI storage table indexing, the key slot in which the key is loaded by using Excrypt Manager is off by one. For example, a key loaded into slot **1** on the Excrypt Manager is referenced in the API as slot **0**.\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| RSA | Enables commands requiring RSA functionality. |\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Keys | View key and table information | Mgmt | 0 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `RD` | Index of the RSA key that is being deleted | Numeric | 1-2 | Yes |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `BQ` | Number of available RSA key slots | Numeric | 2 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `DRSA` |\n\n<a id=\"rd-index-of-the-rsa-key-that-is-being-deleted\"></a>\n\n### RD - Index of the RSA key that is being deleted\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-2 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `DRSA` |\n\n<a id=\"bq-number-of-available-rsa-key-slots\"></a>\n\n### BQ - Number of available RSA key slots\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"command-example\"></a>\n\n## Command example\n\n```\nRequest: [AODRSA;RD20;]\n\nResponse: [AODRSA;BQ80;]\n```\n"
    }
