      "es": "The DUMP command downloads the human readable configuration report from an HSM. The report is returned in chunks across multiple request/response exchanges using a continuation ID. Output is hex-encoded and can be decoded to ASCII text or YAML depending on the `FM` token.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This is a multi-part command. Send the initial request without `CH`, then resend with the `CH` value from each response until `BB` returns `Y`.\n- The configuration report data in `CD` is hex-encoded. Convert to ASCII for a human-readable output.\n- Use `FM1` for YAML format output.",
      "en": "The DUMP command downloads the human readable configuration report from an HSM. The report is returned in chunks across multiple request/response exchanges using a continuation ID. Output is hex-encoded and can be decoded to ASCII text or YAML depending on the `FM` token.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This is a multi-part command. Send the initial request without `CH`, then resend with the `CH` value from each response until `BB` returns `Y`.\n- The configuration report data in `CD` is hex-encoded. Convert to ASCII for a human-readable output.\n- Use `FM1` for YAML format output."
