    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# ECID: Encrypt CID\n\nFuente: [ECID: Encrypt CID](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/data_encryption/symmetric/ecid-encrypt-cid)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:02:28.857Z\n\n---\n\nThis command encrypts hexadecimal-encoded Customer Identification Data (CID).\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The data is encrypted under a Data Encryption Key using Electronic Code Book (ECB) mode.\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| Financial Processing | Enabled by default on all Excrypt Series HSMs and as an add-on license for Vectera Series HSMs. |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `AI` | Data Encryption Key (DEK) | <br><br>Hexadecimal<br><br>ASCII<br><br>Alphanumeric<br><br> | <br><br>16, 32, 48<br><br>74, 88+<br><br>3-7<br><br> | Yes |\n| `AK` | Clear Customer Identification Data (CID) | Hexadecimal | 16, 32, 48 | Yes |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `AK` | Encrypted CID | Hexadecimal | 16, 32, 48 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `ECID` |\n\n<a id=\"ai-data-encryption-key-dek\"></a>\n\n### AI - Data Encryption Key (DEK)\n\nThis field supports the following:\n\n- Cryptogram encrypted under modifier 2 of the MFK\n- AKB or TR-31 key block\n- Key Storage Table index\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16<br>32<br>48 | Hexadecimal | Hexadecimal |\n| 74<br>88+ | ASCII | A - Z, a - z, 0 - 9 except ; [ ] |\n| 3-7 | Alphanumeric | BD + key slot number |\n\n<a id=\"ak-clear-customer-identification-data-cid\"></a>\n\n### AK - Clear Customer Identification Data (CID)\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16<br>32<br>48 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `ECID` |\n\n<a id=\"ak-encrypted-cid\"></a>\n\n### AK - Encrypted CID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16<br>32<br>48 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command Examples\n\n<a id=\"example-1\"></a>\n\n### Example 1\n\n```\nRequest: [AOECID;AIF6216C740478E790F6216C740478E790F6216C740478E790;AK1234567890123456;]\n\nResponse: [AOECID;AK55307DF887BAB5B5;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"example-2\"></a>\n\n### Example 2\n\n```\nRequest: [AOECID;AIB0096D3TN00E000020935E520CEC79DFEB767942204CE2A3A13642F92D36C5B99E96E1F8BAB9D76E2361952CA7564960;AK1234567890123456;]\n\nResponse: [AOECID;AKA8554246F54AC71B;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"test-key-used\"></a>\n\n### Test Key Used\n\nMFK Test Key: D2DE5CD9110F4CAB 1111111111111111 0123456789ABCDEF Check Digit: (financial 8071) (cmac 9652)\n\nDEK\n\n**Cryptogram generated under MFK**\n\nClear component (1 Key part): All 8’s Modifier: DEK Checksum: Standard: 0096 CMAC: 4E13 Parity: Odd Cryptogram: F6216C740478E790F6216C740478E790F6216C740478E790\n\n**Key block generated Under MFK**\n\nClear component (1 Key part): All 8’s Header: B0000D3TN00E0000 Checksum: Standard: F9F4 CMAC: 4F39 Parity: Odd Key Block: B0096D3TN00E000020935E520CEC79DFEB767942204CE2A3A13642F92D36C5B99E96E1F8BAB9D76E2361952CA7564960\n",
      "en": "# ECID: Encrypt CID\n\nFuente: [ECID: Encrypt CID](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/data_encryption/symmetric/ecid-encrypt-cid)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:02:28.857Z\n\n---\n\nThis command encrypts hexadecimal-encoded Customer Identification Data (CID).\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The data is encrypted under a Data Encryption Key using Electronic Code Book (ECB) mode.\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| Financial Processing | Enabled by default on all Excrypt Series HSMs and as an add-on license for Vectera Series HSMs. |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `AI` | Data Encryption Key (DEK) | <br><br>Hexadecimal<br><br>ASCII<br><br>Alphanumeric<br><br> | <br><br>16, 32, 48<br><br>74, 88+<br><br>3-7<br><br> | Yes |\n| `AK` | Clear Customer Identification Data (CID) | Hexadecimal | 16, 32, 48 | Yes |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `AK` | Encrypted CID | Hexadecimal | 16, 32, 48 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `ECID` |\n\n<a id=\"ai-data-encryption-key-dek\"></a>\n\n### AI - Data Encryption Key (DEK)\n\nThis field supports the following:\n\n- Cryptogram encrypted under modifier 2 of the MFK\n- AKB or TR-31 key block\n- Key Storage Table index\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16<br>32<br>48 | Hexadecimal | Hexadecimal |\n| 74<br>88+ | ASCII | A - Z, a - z, 0 - 9 except ; [ ] |\n| 3-7 | Alphanumeric | BD + key slot number |\n\n<a id=\"ak-clear-customer-identification-data-cid\"></a>\n\n### AK - Clear Customer Identification Data (CID)\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16<br>32<br>48 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `ECID` |\n\n<a id=\"ak-encrypted-cid\"></a>\n\n### AK - Encrypted CID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16<br>32<br>48 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command Examples\n\n<a id=\"example-1\"></a>\n\n### Example 1\n\n```\nRequest: [AOECID;AIF6216C740478E790F6216C740478E790F6216C740478E790;AK1234567890123456;]\n\nResponse: [AOECID;AK55307DF887BAB5B5;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"example-2\"></a>\n\n### Example 2\n\n```\nRequest: [AOECID;AIB0096D3TN00E000020935E520CEC79DFEB767942204CE2A3A13642F92D36C5B99E96E1F8BAB9D76E2361952CA7564960;AK1234567890123456;]\n\nResponse: [AOECID;AKA8554246F54AC71B;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"test-key-used\"></a>\n\n### Test Key Used\n\nMFK Test Key: D2DE5CD9110F4CAB 1111111111111111 0123456789ABCDEF Check Digit: (financial 8071) (cmac 9652)\n\nDEK\n\n**Cryptogram generated under MFK**\n\nClear component (1 Key part): All 8’s Modifier: DEK Checksum: Standard: 0096 CMAC: 4E13 Parity: Odd Cryptogram: F6216C740478E790F6216C740478E790F6216C740478E790\n\n**Key block generated Under MFK**\n\nClear component (1 Key part): All 8’s Header: B0000D3TN00E0000 Checksum: Standard: F9F4 CMAC: 4F39 Parity: Odd Key Block: B0096D3TN00E000020935E520CEC79DFEB767942204CE2A3A13642F92D36C5B99E96E1F8BAB9D76E2361952CA7564960\n"
    }
