    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# EDAT: Encrypt Data\n\nFuente: [EDAT: Encrypt Data](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/data_encryption/symmetric/edat-encrypt-data)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:02:29.967Z\n\n---\n\nThis command encrypts arbitrary hexadecimal data.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- Command **DDAT** reverses this command to return encrypted data to its clear form.\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| Financial Processing | Enabled by default on all Excrypt Series HSMs and as an add-on license for Vectera Series HSMs. |\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Management Commands:Crypto | Gives permission to perform basic crypto operations on the administrative port. | Mgmt | 1 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `EDAT` |\n\n<a id=\"ai-data-encryption-key-dek\"></a>\n\n### AI - Data Encryption Key (DEK)\n\nThis field supports the following:\n\n- Cryptogram encrypted under modifier 2 of the MFK\n- AKB or TR-31 key block\n- Key Storage Table index\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16<br>32<br>48 | Hexadecimal | Hexadecimal |\n| 74<br>88+ | ASCII | A - Z, a - z, 0 - 9 except ; [ ] |\n| 3-7 | Alphanumeric | BD + key slot number |\n\n<a id=\"ak-data-to-be-encrypted\"></a>\n\n### AK - Data to be encrypted\n\nMust be in multiples of 16.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16-2048 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id-2\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `EDAT` |\n\n<a id=\"ak-encrypted-data\"></a>\n\n### AK - Encrypted data\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16-2048 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"command-rxamples\"></a>\n\n## Command rxamples\n\n<a id=\"example-1\"></a>\n\n### Example 1\n\n```\nRequest: [AOEDAT;AI54CB448FCF15ADB6;AKEE6B6E02F37A28CB;]\n\nResponse: [AOEDAT;AK29902A7676FFC2BD;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"example-2\"></a>\n\n### Example 2\n\n```\nRequest: [AOEDAT;AIBD27;AKEE6B6E02F37A28CB;AGSample context field message;]\n\nResponse: [AOEDAT;AK29902A7676FFC2BD;AGSample context field message;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"example-3\"></a>\n\n### Example 3\n\n```\nRequest: [AOEDAT;AIB0096D3TN00E000020935E520CEC79DFEB767942204CE2A3A13642F92D36C5B99E96E1F8BAB9D76E2361952CA7564960;AKEE6B6E02F37A28CB;]\n\nResponse: [AOEDAT;AKBD12C26809A8738C;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"test-key-used\"></a>\n\n### Test Key Used\n\nMFK Test Key: D2DE5CD9110F4CAB 1111111111111111 0123456789ABCDEF Check Digit: (financial 8071) (cmac 9652)\n\n**Key block generated**\n\nClear component (1 Key part): All 8’s Header: B0000D3TN00E0000 Checksum: Standard: F9F4 CMAC: 4F39 Parity: Odd Key Block: B0096D3TN00E000020935E520CEC79DFEB767942204CE2A3A13642F92D36C5B99E96E1F8BAB9D76E2361952CA7564960\n",
      "en": "# EDAT: Encrypt Data\n\nFuente: [EDAT: Encrypt Data](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/data_encryption/symmetric/edat-encrypt-data)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:02:29.967Z\n\n---\n\nThis command encrypts arbitrary hexadecimal data.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- Command **DDAT** reverses this command to return encrypted data to its clear form.\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| Financial Processing | Enabled by default on all Excrypt Series HSMs and as an add-on license for Vectera Series HSMs. |\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Management Commands:Crypto | Gives permission to perform basic crypto operations on the administrative port. | Mgmt | 1 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `EDAT` |\n\n<a id=\"ai-data-encryption-key-dek\"></a>\n\n### AI - Data Encryption Key (DEK)\n\nThis field supports the following:\n\n- Cryptogram encrypted under modifier 2 of the MFK\n- AKB or TR-31 key block\n- Key Storage Table index\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16<br>32<br>48 | Hexadecimal | Hexadecimal |\n| 74<br>88+ | ASCII | A - Z, a - z, 0 - 9 except ; [ ] |\n| 3-7 | Alphanumeric | BD + key slot number |\n\n<a id=\"ak-data-to-be-encrypted\"></a>\n\n### AK - Data to be encrypted\n\nMust be in multiples of 16.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16-2048 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id-2\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `EDAT` |\n\n<a id=\"ak-encrypted-data\"></a>\n\n### AK - Encrypted data\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16-2048 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"command-rxamples\"></a>\n\n## Command rxamples\n\n<a id=\"example-1\"></a>\n\n### Example 1\n\n```\nRequest: [AOEDAT;AI54CB448FCF15ADB6;AKEE6B6E02F37A28CB;]\n\nResponse: [AOEDAT;AK29902A7676FFC2BD;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"example-2\"></a>\n\n### Example 2\n\n```\nRequest: [AOEDAT;AIBD27;AKEE6B6E02F37A28CB;AGSample context field message;]\n\nResponse: [AOEDAT;AK29902A7676FFC2BD;AGSample context field message;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"example-3\"></a>\n\n### Example 3\n\n```\nRequest: [AOEDAT;AIB0096D3TN00E000020935E520CEC79DFEB767942204CE2A3A13642F92D36C5B99E96E1F8BAB9D76E2361952CA7564960;AKEE6B6E02F37A28CB;]\n\nResponse: [AOEDAT;AKBD12C26809A8738C;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"test-key-used\"></a>\n\n### Test Key Used\n\nMFK Test Key: D2DE5CD9110F4CAB 1111111111111111 0123456789ABCDEF Check Digit: (financial 8071) (cmac 9652)\n\n**Key block generated**\n\nClear component (1 Key part): All 8’s Header: B0000D3TN00E0000 Checksum: Standard: F9F4 CMAC: 4F39 Parity: Odd Key Block: B0096D3TN00E000020935E520CEC79DFEB767942204CE2A3A13642F92D36C5B99E96E1F8BAB9D76E2361952CA7564960\n"
    }
