      "en": "FLPY computes a five-digit Modsia authentication code over an ASCII message (`AK`) keyed by a message authentication key (`BT`) and modified by a nine-digit variable number (`YO`). The MAK is supplied as a cryptogram under the MAK modifier (`03`) of the chosen major key, or as a TR-31/TR-31 key block with a MAC-generate usage; `FS` selects which major key (`FS1` MFK, `FS6` PMK, `FS7` FTK) protects that key, and it must match the major key the cryptogram was wrapped under or the HSM returns `AM48 INVALID KEYBLOCK` / `AM47 INVALID MAC`. The variable number `YO` feeds into the derivation, so the same key and message produce a different code for each `YO`. The result is returned in a single `AC` token. Unlike the general-purpose MAC generators [GMAC](gmac-generate-mac.md) and [GPMC](gpmc-general-purpose-symmetric-mac.md), FLPY implements the fixed Modsia scheme and always returns a five-digit decimal code rather than a configurable-length hex MAC.\n\n**Available in firmware version 7.6.1.36 and later.**\n\n> **Warning:** Disabled in PCI HSM mode pending PCI approval\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The `AK` message length must be a multiple of 8; otherwise the HSM returns `AM13 INVALID MESSAGE LENGTH`.\n- `FS` is required on this firmware. Omitting it returns `AM04 TOKEN MISSING`."
