    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# FPTY: Force Parity of Existing Key\n\nFuente: [FPTY: Force Parity of Existing Key](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/lifecycle/fpty-force-parity-of-existing-key)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:02:44.295Z\n\n---\n\nThis command forces the parity of an existing DES/TDES key to either ODD or EVEN.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS mode\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-format\"></a>\n\n## Request Format\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-indicator\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Indicator\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `FPTY` |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-major-key-of-input-cryptogram\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - Major key of input cryptogram\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: MFK<br>`6`: PMK (Default)<br>`7`: FTK (if PKCS11 is available) |\n\n<a id=\"send-either-token-bd-or-bg-and-as\"></a>\n\n### Send either token BD or BG and AS.\n\n<a id=\"optional-bd-key-slot-to-force-parity-on\"></a>\n\n#### (Optional) BD - Key slot to force parity on\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | `0-4000` |\n\n<a id=\"optional-bg-cryptogram-of-a-symmetric-key-under-major-key-to-force-parity-on\"></a>\n\n#### (Optional) BG - Cryptogram of a symmetric key under major key to force parity on\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16-128 | Hexadecimal | `0-9, A-F` |\n\n<a id=\"optional-as-modifier-of-token-bg\"></a>\n\n#### (Optional) AS - Modifier of token BG\n\nSend with Token **BG**.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-2 | Hexadecimal | `0`: Key Encryption Key (KEK)<br>`1`: PIN Encryption Key (PEK)<br>`2`: Data Encryption Key (DEK)<br>`3`: Message Authentication Key (MAK)<br>`4`: PIN Verification Key (PVK)<br>`8`: Base Derivation Key (BDK)<br>`9`: PIN Generation Key (PGK)<br>`E`: Detachment Derivation Key |\n\n<a id=\"optional-rt-parity-to-force-key-to\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) RT - Parity to force key to\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `0`: NONE<br>`1`: ODD (default)<br>`2`: EVEN |\n\n<a id=\"response-format\"></a>\n\n## Response Format\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-indicator\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response Indicator\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `FPTY` |\n\n<a id=\"ae-check-digit\"></a>\n\n### AE - Check digit\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"bg-new-cryptogram\"></a>\n\n### BG - New cryptogram\n\nNot returned if request token BD is sent.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16+ | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command Examples\n\n**ODD To EVEN Parity**\n\n```\nRequest: [AOFPTY;FS1;BGB882D89D272C806EB882D89D272C806EB882D89D272C806E;AS1;RT2;]\n\nResponse: [AOFPTY;AE0F2F;BG237F02BAD8CE2EB0237F02BAD8CE2EB0237F02BAD8CE2EB0;]\n```\n\n**EVEN To ODD Parity**\n\n```\nRequest: [AOFPTY;FS1;BG237F02BAD8CE2EB0237F02BAD8CE2EB0237F02BAD8CE2EB0;AS1;RT1;]\n\nResponse: [AOFPTY;AE0F2F;BGB882D89D272C806EB882D89D272C806EB882D89D272C806E;]\n```\n\n**Test Key Used**\n\nMFK Test Key: D2DE5CD9110F4CAB 1111111111111111 0123456789ABCDEF Check Digit: (financial 8071) (cmac 9652)\n\n2025-07-23\n\n- Fixed **FW-16936** | Resolved an issue where the key type was not being validated against the security policy when attempting to modify a key slot.\n",
      "en": "# FPTY: Force Parity of Existing Key\n\nFuente: [FPTY: Force Parity of Existing Key](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/lifecycle/fpty-force-parity-of-existing-key)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:02:44.295Z\n\n---\n\nThis command forces the parity of an existing DES/TDES key to either ODD or EVEN.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS mode\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-format\"></a>\n\n## Request Format\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-indicator\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Indicator\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `FPTY` |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-major-key-of-input-cryptogram\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - Major key of input cryptogram\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: MFK<br>`6`: PMK (Default)<br>`7`: FTK (if PKCS11 is available) |\n\n<a id=\"send-either-token-bd-or-bg-and-as\"></a>\n\n### Send either token BD or BG and AS.\n\n<a id=\"optional-bd-key-slot-to-force-parity-on\"></a>\n\n#### (Optional) BD - Key slot to force parity on\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | `0-4000` |\n\n<a id=\"optional-bg-cryptogram-of-a-symmetric-key-under-major-key-to-force-parity-on\"></a>\n\n#### (Optional) BG - Cryptogram of a symmetric key under major key to force parity on\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16-128 | Hexadecimal | `0-9, A-F` |\n\n<a id=\"optional-as-modifier-of-token-bg\"></a>\n\n#### (Optional) AS - Modifier of token BG\n\nSend with Token **BG**.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-2 | Hexadecimal | `0`: Key Encryption Key (KEK)<br>`1`: PIN Encryption Key (PEK)<br>`2`: Data Encryption Key (DEK)<br>`3`: Message Authentication Key (MAK)<br>`4`: PIN Verification Key (PVK)<br>`8`: Base Derivation Key (BDK)<br>`9`: PIN Generation Key (PGK)<br>`E`: Detachment Derivation Key |\n\n<a id=\"optional-rt-parity-to-force-key-to\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) RT - Parity to force key to\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `0`: NONE<br>`1`: ODD (default)<br>`2`: EVEN |\n\n<a id=\"response-format\"></a>\n\n## Response Format\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-indicator\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response Indicator\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `FPTY` |\n\n<a id=\"ae-check-digit\"></a>\n\n### AE - Check digit\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"bg-new-cryptogram\"></a>\n\n### BG - New cryptogram\n\nNot returned if request token BD is sent.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16+ | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command Examples\n\n**ODD To EVEN Parity**\n\n```\nRequest: [AOFPTY;FS1;BGB882D89D272C806EB882D89D272C806EB882D89D272C806E;AS1;RT2;]\n\nResponse: [AOFPTY;AE0F2F;BG237F02BAD8CE2EB0237F02BAD8CE2EB0237F02BAD8CE2EB0;]\n```\n\n**EVEN To ODD Parity**\n\n```\nRequest: [AOFPTY;FS1;BG237F02BAD8CE2EB0237F02BAD8CE2EB0237F02BAD8CE2EB0;AS1;RT1;]\n\nResponse: [AOFPTY;AE0F2F;BGB882D89D272C806EB882D89D272C806EB882D89D272C806E;]\n```\n\n**Test Key Used**\n\nMFK Test Key: D2DE5CD9110F4CAB 1111111111111111 0123456789ABCDEF Check Digit: (financial 8071) (cmac 9652)\n\n2025-07-23\n\n- Fixed **FW-16936** | Resolved an issue where the key type was not being validated against the security policy when attempting to modify a key slot.\n"
    }
