    "name": {
      "es": "GCKD: Generate Check Digits",
      "en": "GCKD: Generate Check Digits"
    },
    "summary": {
      "es": "This command computes the check digits, or key check value (KCV), of a working key supplied in `BG` as a cryptogram, an AKB or TR-31 key block, or a key-storage-table index. Token `FU` selects the algorithm (Futurex, IBM, standard financial, Visa, or CMAC), except for HMAC key blocks, where the algorithm is fixed and `FU` is ignored. The KCV is returned in `AE`. Token `AD` widens the result for both AES and 3DES keys, up to 6 characters under `FUF`, `FUS`, and `FUC` on a 3DES key, and up to 10 under `FUC` on an AES key. `FUV` accepts only its fixed width of 6, `FUI` only 4, and `FUI` rejects AES keys outright with `AM03 ANFU VALUE OUT OF RANGE`.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This command enables each key holder to calculate the check digits for a cryptogram if the check digits are not available, by using the appropriate algorithm.\n- If generating check digits for a key block, you must enable the TR-31 and AKB options.",
      "en": "This command computes the check digits, or key check value (KCV), of a working key supplied in `BG` as a cryptogram, an AKB or TR-31 key block, or a key-storage-table index. Token `FU` selects the algorithm (Futurex, IBM, standard financial, Visa, or CMAC), except for HMAC key blocks, where the algorithm is fixed and `FU` is ignored. The KCV is returned in `AE`. Token `AD` widens the result for both AES and 3DES keys, up to 6 characters under `FUF`, `FUS`, and `FUC` on a 3DES key, and up to 10 under `FUC` on an AES key. `FUV` accepts only its fixed width of 6, `FUI` only 4, and `FUI` rejects AES keys outright with `AM03 ANFU VALUE OUT OF RANGE`.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This command enables each key holder to calculate the check digits for a cryptogram if the check digits are not available, by using the appropriate algorithm.\n- If generating check digits for a key block, you must enable the TR-31 and AKB options."
    },
    "description": {
      "es": "This command computes the check digits, or key check value (KCV), of a working key supplied in `BG` as a cryptogram, an AKB or TR-31 key block, or a key-storage-table index. Token `FU` selects the algorithm (Futurex, IBM, standard financial, Visa, or CMAC), except for HMAC key blocks, where the algorithm is fixed and `FU` is ignored. The KCV is returned in `AE`. Token `AD` widens the result for both AES and 3DES keys, up to 6 characters under `FUF`, `FUS`, and `FUC` on a 3DES key, and up to 10 under `FUC` on an AES key. `FUV` accepts only its fixed width of 6, `FUI` only 4, and `FUI` rejects AES keys outright with `AM03 ANFU VALUE OUT OF RANGE`.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This command enables each key holder to calculate the check digits for a cryptogram if the check digits are not available, by using the appropriate algorithm.\n- If generating check digits for a key block, you must enable the TR-31 and AKB options.",
      "en": "This command computes the check digits, or key check value (KCV), of a working key supplied in `BG` as a cryptogram, an AKB or TR-31 key block, or a key-storage-table index. Token `FU` selects the algorithm (Futurex, IBM, standard financial, Visa, or CMAC), except for HMAC key blocks, where the algorithm is fixed and `FU` is ignored. The KCV is returned in `AE`. Token `AD` widens the result for both AES and 3DES keys, up to 6 characters under `FUF`, `FUS`, and `FUC` on a 3DES key, and up to 10 under `FUC` on an AES key. `FUV` accepts only its fixed width of 6, `FUI` only 4, and `FUI` rejects AES keys outright with `AM03 ANFU VALUE OUT OF RANGE`.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This command enables each key holder to calculate the check digits for a cryptogram if the check digits are not available, by using the appropriate algorithm.\n- If generating check digits for a key block, you must enable the TR-31 and AKB options."
    },
