    "name": {
      "es": "GCRT: Get certificate from index or connection pair",
      "en": "GCRT: Get certificate from index or connection pair"
    },
    "summary": {
      "es": "GCRT retrieves a stored certificate from the HSM by specifying either a certificate index or an SSL2TCP connection pair. The caller can choose between hex-encoded DER output and a Base64-encoded certificate description by setting the BA token. When using a connection pair, the TP and CS tokens select the pair index and the client or server side; when using a certificate index, only the CI token is needed. Use LCRT to load a certificate before retrieving it with GCRT.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- If both CI and TP are omitted, the command will return an error. CI takes precedence when both are sent.\n- The default encoding is hex-encoded DER (`BA0`). Send `BA1` for Base64-encoded certificate description.",
      "en": "GCRT retrieves a stored certificate from the HSM by specifying either a certificate index or an SSL2TCP connection pair. The caller can choose between hex-encoded DER output and a Base64-encoded certificate description by setting the BA token. When using a connection pair, the TP and CS tokens select the pair index and the client or server side; when using a certificate index, only the CI token is needed. Use LCRT to load a certificate before retrieving it with GCRT.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- If both CI and TP are omitted, the command will return an error. CI takes precedence when both are sent.\n- The default encoding is hex-encoded DER (`BA0`). Send `BA1` for Base64-encoded certificate description."
    },
    "description": {
      "es": "GCRT retrieves a stored certificate from the HSM by specifying either a certificate index or an SSL2TCP connection pair. The caller can choose between hex-encoded DER output and a Base64-encoded certificate description by setting the BA token. When using a connection pair, the TP and CS tokens select the pair index and the client or server side; when using a certificate index, only the CI token is needed. Use LCRT to load a certificate before retrieving it with GCRT.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- If both CI and TP are omitted, the command will return an error. CI takes precedence when both are sent.\n- The default encoding is hex-encoded DER (`BA0`). Send `BA1` for Base64-encoded certificate description.",
      "en": "GCRT retrieves a stored certificate from the HSM by specifying either a certificate index or an SSL2TCP connection pair. The caller can choose between hex-encoded DER output and a Base64-encoded certificate description by setting the BA token. When using a connection pair, the TP and CS tokens select the pair index and the client or server side; when using a certificate index, only the CI token is needed. Use LCRT to load a certificate before retrieving it with GCRT.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- If both CI and TP are omitted, the command will return an error. CI takes precedence when both are sent.\n- The default encoding is hex-encoded DER (`BA0`). Send `BA1` for Base64-encoded certificate description."
    },
