    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# GIDN: Generate an ICC dynamic number (IDN)\n\nFuente: [GIDN: Generate an ICC dynamic number (IDN)](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/payments_cards/emv/acquiring/gidn-generate-an-icc-dynamic-number-idn)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:03:39.890Z\n\n---\n\nThis command generates an ICC dynamic number (IDN) by using the EMV ICC Master Dynamic Number Key encrypted under modifier 1B of the Master File Key to encrypt the application transaction number padded with zeros up to 16 characters.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- EMV ICC Master Dynamic Number Key is derived with the standard EMV CSK method, using PAN and PAN Sequence Number.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS mode\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| EMV Acquiring | Enables the Europay Mastercard Visa (EMV) acquiring command set. EMV is a global standard for card-based transactions. |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `GIDN` |\n\n<a id=\"ca-emv-icc-master-dynamic-number-key\"></a>\n\n### CA - EMV ICC Master Dynamic Number Key\n\nThis field supports the following formats:\n\n- Cryptogram encrypted under modifier 1B of the MFK\n- AKB or TR-31 key block\n- Key Storage Table index\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16<br>32<br>48 | Hexadecimal | **Cryptogram**<br>0 - 9, A - F |\n| 74<br>88+ | ASCII | **Key block**<br>A - Z, a - z, 0 - 9 except ; [ ] |\n| 3-7 | Alphanumeric | BD + key slot number |\n\n<a id=\"bz-application-pan\"></a>\n\n### BZ - Application PAN\n\nThis field has no padding with `F` characters.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-19 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"kr-application-pan-sequence-number\"></a>\n\n### KR - Application PAN Sequence Number\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"ks-application-transaction-number-atc\"></a>\n\n### KS - Application Transaction Number (ATC)\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `GIDN` |\n\n<a id=\"fc-idn\"></a>\n\n### FC - IDN\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"ae-issuer-master-key-check-value\"></a>\n\n### AE - Issuer Master Key Check Value\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4-6 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"kx-idn-icc-master-key-check-value\"></a>\n\n### KX - IDN ICC Master Key Check Value\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4-6 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n**IDN Format Notes**\n\n```\nIDN = 3DES(ICC MK_IDN) [ ATC_1 || ATC_0 || 00 || 00 || 00 || 00 || 00 || 00 ]\n```\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command Examples\n\n```\nRequest: [AOGIDN;BZ1234567890123456789;KR61;KS1234;CAEFF3DBA36C87199F12533EB99F5CDDFE;]\n\nResponse: [AOGIDN;FC0601FDB152FBF361;AE5001;KX5CD0;]\n```\n\n```\nRequest: [AOGIDN;BZ1234567890123456789;KR61;KS1234;CAA0088E4TX00E0000628FF310F0725E3ECF9379FE9FAA9FC6B872277DA77620B9866005586E15D910E4C5B0C8;]\n\nResponse: [AOGIDN;FC0601FDB152FBF361;AE5001;KX5CD0;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"test-key-used\"></a>\n\n### Test Key Used\n\nMFK Test Key: D2DE5CD9110F4CAB 1111111111111111 0123456789ABCDEF Check Digit: (financial 8071) (cmac 9652)\n",
      "en": "# GIDN: Generate an ICC dynamic number (IDN)\n\nFuente: [GIDN: Generate an ICC dynamic number (IDN)](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/payments_cards/emv/acquiring/gidn-generate-an-icc-dynamic-number-idn)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:03:39.890Z\n\n---\n\nThis command generates an ICC dynamic number (IDN) by using the EMV ICC Master Dynamic Number Key encrypted under modifier 1B of the Master File Key to encrypt the application transaction number padded with zeros up to 16 characters.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- EMV ICC Master Dynamic Number Key is derived with the standard EMV CSK method, using PAN and PAN Sequence Number.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS mode\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| EMV Acquiring | Enables the Europay Mastercard Visa (EMV) acquiring command set. EMV is a global standard for card-based transactions. |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `GIDN` |\n\n<a id=\"ca-emv-icc-master-dynamic-number-key\"></a>\n\n### CA - EMV ICC Master Dynamic Number Key\n\nThis field supports the following formats:\n\n- Cryptogram encrypted under modifier 1B of the MFK\n- AKB or TR-31 key block\n- Key Storage Table index\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16<br>32<br>48 | Hexadecimal | **Cryptogram**<br>0 - 9, A - F |\n| 74<br>88+ | ASCII | **Key block**<br>A - Z, a - z, 0 - 9 except ; [ ] |\n| 3-7 | Alphanumeric | BD + key slot number |\n\n<a id=\"bz-application-pan\"></a>\n\n### BZ - Application PAN\n\nThis field has no padding with `F` characters.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-19 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"kr-application-pan-sequence-number\"></a>\n\n### KR - Application PAN Sequence Number\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"ks-application-transaction-number-atc\"></a>\n\n### KS - Application Transaction Number (ATC)\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `GIDN` |\n\n<a id=\"fc-idn\"></a>\n\n### FC - IDN\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"ae-issuer-master-key-check-value\"></a>\n\n### AE - Issuer Master Key Check Value\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4-6 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"kx-idn-icc-master-key-check-value\"></a>\n\n### KX - IDN ICC Master Key Check Value\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4-6 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n**IDN Format Notes**\n\n```\nIDN = 3DES(ICC MK_IDN) [ ATC_1 || ATC_0 || 00 || 00 || 00 || 00 || 00 || 00 ]\n```\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command Examples\n\n```\nRequest: [AOGIDN;BZ1234567890123456789;KR61;KS1234;CAEFF3DBA36C87199F12533EB99F5CDDFE;]\n\nResponse: [AOGIDN;FC0601FDB152FBF361;AE5001;KX5CD0;]\n```\n\n```\nRequest: [AOGIDN;BZ1234567890123456789;KR61;KS1234;CAA0088E4TX00E0000628FF310F0725E3ECF9379FE9FAA9FC6B872277DA77620B9866005586E15D910E4C5B0C8;]\n\nResponse: [AOGIDN;FC0601FDB152FBF361;AE5001;KX5CD0;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"test-key-used\"></a>\n\n### Test Key Used\n\nMFK Test Key: D2DE5CD9110F4CAB 1111111111111111 0123456789ABCDEF Check Digit: (financial 8071) (cmac 9652)\n"
    }
