    "summary": {
      "es": "This command generates a key block from a custom header. However, unlike command **GKBL**, this command does not allow changing the modifier of a cryptogram unless under dual control.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- If you do not supply a Key Encryption Key (KEK), the MFK encrypts the working key.\n- If you provide a KEK and plan to use it to translate a symmetric key, then token **BG** is assumed to be under that KEK mod **AS**.\n- If you provide a KEK, the output key block is under the KEK.\n- Support for generating AES AKB key blocks is available in FW 7.6.1.31 and later.",
      "en": "This command generates a key block from a custom header. However, unlike command **GKBL**, this command does not allow changing the modifier of a cryptogram unless under dual control.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- If you do not supply a Key Encryption Key (KEK), the MFK encrypts the working key.\n- If you provide a KEK and plan to use it to translate a symmetric key, then token **BG** is assumed to be under that KEK mod **AS**.\n- If you provide a KEK, the output key block is under the KEK.\n- Support for generating AES AKB key blocks is available in FW 7.6.1.31 and later."
    },
