    "description": {
      "es": "This command generates a key block from a modifier-based cryptogram.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- Can be used to translate asymmetric cryptograms.\n- If you do not provide a Key Encryption Key (KEK), the MFK encrypts the working key.\n- If you provide a KEK and it’s going to translate a symmetric key, then token **BG** is assumed to be under that KEK using the modifier specified in token **AS**.\n- If you provide a KEK, the output key block is under the KEK.\n- The output key block is always encrypted under modifier 0.\n- If using application partitions, then you must enable the **Keys:No Usage Wrap** permission.\n- For TR-31 key blocks, all Optional Blocks in the key block must be a multiple of the encryption block length. If it’s not, it is padded with a PB padding block with an appropriate number of padding characters.\n- Support for generating AES AKB key blocks is available in FW 7.6.1.31 and later.\n- Translation of an AKB CA public key with header `1RRVN00k` to TR-31 is available in FW 7.6.1.35 and later.",
      "en": "This command generates a key block from a modifier-based cryptogram.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- Can be used to translate asymmetric cryptograms.\n- If you do not provide a Key Encryption Key (KEK), the MFK encrypts the working key.\n- If you provide a KEK and it’s going to translate a symmetric key, then token **BG** is assumed to be under that KEK using the modifier specified in token **AS**.\n- If you provide a KEK, the output key block is under the KEK.\n- The output key block is always encrypted under modifier 0.\n- If using application partitions, then you must enable the **Keys:No Usage Wrap** permission.\n- For TR-31 key blocks, all Optional Blocks in the key block must be a multiple of the encryption block length. If it’s not, it is padded with a PB padding block with an appropriate number of padding characters.\n- Support for generating AES AKB key blocks is available in FW 7.6.1.31 and later.\n- Translation of an AKB CA public key with header `1RRVN00k` to TR-31 is available in FW 7.6.1.35 and later."
    },
