      "en": "This command generates a message authentication code (MAC).\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- Includes two formats: regular and binary mode. Binary mode allows you to send hex-encoded data, which is decoded before calculating the MAC.\n- Added in FW 7.4.1.17 configuration setting *Strict MAC TR31 Usage* under Key Management on the Web Portal to enforce TR-31 key usage.\n- By default, the maximum length of an Excrypt request message is 15,360 characters. For request token **BO**, the **Max Tag Length** can be as large as the max request message length supports after factoring in all other message parts. You can change the **Max Request Message Length** setting in the HSM Web Portal or the Excrypt Manager application."
