    "pairedCode": "GNOF",
    "name": {
      "es": "GNOF: Generate New Offset",
      "en": "GNOF: Generate New Offset"
    },
    "summary": {
      "es": "This command generates a new offset for a new card while keeping the same customer PIN, using the IBM 3624 PIN generation method.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in PCI HSM mode when Clear PIN license is enabled.\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- You can use the current data for tokens **AY**, **BE**, and **BS** for new data in the tokens **FL**, **FM**, and **FN**. For example, the current decimalization table (token **BS**) can also be the new decimalization table (token **FL**).\n- Right or left justification of the offset is selected by token **BF**.  \n\n  - If right-justification is selected (**BF2**), then token **AD**must contain the length of the current customer PIN.\n  - If left-justification is selected (**BF0**), then the offset length will equal the length of the customer PIN.",
      "en": "This command generates a new offset for a new card while keeping the same customer PIN, using the IBM 3624 PIN generation method.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in PCI HSM mode when Clear PIN license is enabled.\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- You can use the current data for tokens **AY**, **BE**, and **BS** for new data in the tokens **FL**, **FM**, and **FN**. For example, the current decimalization table (token **BS**) can also be the new decimalization table (token **FL**).\n- Right or left justification of the offset is selected by token **BF**.  \n\n  - If right-justification is selected (**BF2**), then token **AD**must contain the length of the current customer PIN.\n  - If left-justification is selected (**BF0**), then the offset length will equal the length of the customer PIN."
    },
    "description": {
      "es": "This command generates a new offset for a new card while keeping the same customer PIN, using the IBM 3624 PIN generation method.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in PCI HSM mode when Clear PIN license is enabled.\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- You can use the current data for tokens **AY**, **BE**, and **BS** for new data in the tokens **FL**, **FM**, and **FN**. For example, the current decimalization table (token **BS**) can also be the new decimalization table (token **FL**).\n- Right or left justification of the offset is selected by token **BF**.  \n\n  - If right-justification is selected (**BF2**), then token **AD**must contain the length of the current customer PIN.\n  - If left-justification is selected (**BF0**), then the offset length will equal the length of the customer PIN.",
      "en": "This command generates a new offset for a new card while keeping the same customer PIN, using the IBM 3624 PIN generation method.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in PCI HSM mode when Clear PIN license is enabled.\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- You can use the current data for tokens **AY**, **BE**, and **BS** for new data in the tokens **FL**, **FM**, and **FN**. For example, the current decimalization table (token **BS**) can also be the new decimalization table (token **FL**).\n- Right or left justification of the offset is selected by token **BF**.  \n\n  - If right-justification is selected (**BF2**), then token **AD**must contain the length of the current customer PIN.\n  - If left-justification is selected (**BF0**), then the offset length will equal the length of the customer PIN."
    },
