    "summary": {
      "es": "This command decrypts data by using the GCM cipher.\n\n`AI` also accepts a TR-31 (ANSI X9.143) `D0` key block in place of the raw cryptogram. The block’s header is enforced: the key’s algorithm must be AES and its mode of use must permit decryption (`D` decrypt-only or `B` both). An encrypt-only (`E`) block returns `AM73 HEADER MISMATCH`.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- `AI` accepts either an AES key wrapped under modifier `2` of the major key, or a TR-31 `D0` key block whose header authorizes AES decryption (mode of use `D` or `B`). An encrypt-only (`E`) block or a non-AES algorithm returns `AM73 HEADER MISMATCH`.\n- By default, the maximum length of an Excrypt request message is 15,360 characters. For request tokens **BO**and **AA,** you can configure the **Max Tag Length** between **15360**(default) and **512032**with the **Max Request Message Length** setting by using the HSM Web Portal or the Excrypt Manager application.",
      "en": "This command decrypts data by using the GCM cipher.\n\n`AI` also accepts a TR-31 (ANSI X9.143) `D0` key block in place of the raw cryptogram. The block’s header is enforced: the key’s algorithm must be AES and its mode of use must permit decryption (`D` decrypt-only or `B` both). An encrypt-only (`E`) block returns `AM73 HEADER MISMATCH`.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- `AI` accepts either an AES key wrapped under modifier `2` of the major key, or a TR-31 `D0` key block whose header authorizes AES decryption (mode of use `D` or `B`). An encrypt-only (`E`) block or a non-AES algorithm returns `AM73 HEADER MISMATCH`.\n- By default, the maximum length of an Excrypt request message is 15,360 characters. For request tokens **BO**and **AA,** you can configure the **Max Tag Length** between **15360**(default) and **512032**with the **Max Request Message Length** setting by using the HSM Web Portal or the Excrypt Manager application."
    },
