      "es": "This command encrypts any number of bytes by using subsequent requests (updates) that use the GCM cipher.\n\n`AI` also accepts a TR-31 (ANSI X9.143) `D0` key block in place of the raw cryptogram. The block’s header is enforced: the key’s algorithm must be AES and its mode of use must permit encryption (`E` encrypt-only or `B` both). A decrypt-only (`D`) block returns `AM73 HEADER MISMATCH`.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The additional authenticated data (AAD) must be processed before any plaintext data is processed. Either all data goes in the same **GPAE** request, or you send a continuation request. In the first request, you send the AAD, and then after you send all the AAD data, send the plaintext.\n- `AI` accepts either an AES key wrapped under modifier `2` of the major key, or a TR-31 `D0` key block whose header authorizes AES encryption (mode of use `E` or `B`). A decrypt-only (`D`) block or a non-AES algorithm returns `AM73 HEADER MISMATCH`.\n- The number of max **GPAE** contexts that you can create is 1,000.\n- By default, the maximum length of an Excrypt request message is 15,360 characters. For request tokens **BO**and **AA,** you can configure the **Max Tag Length**between **15360**(default) and **512032**with the **Max Request Message Length** setting using the HSM Web Portal or the Excrypt Manager application.",
