    "summary": {
      "es": "GPEA encrypts the hexadecimal plaintext in `BO` with the RSA public key in `RC`. The `2-6144` range is the protocol field limit, not the RSA plaintext capacity. `CE1` (PKCS #1 v1.5, default) allows at most `k - 11` plaintext bytes, where `k` is the RSA modulus length in bytes. `CE4` (OAEP) allows at most `k - (2 × hLen) - 2` bytes, where `hLen` is the selected hash length. `CE0` requires plaintext exactly as long as the modulus.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- `BO` must contain an even number of hexadecimal characters. Odd-length values return `AM13 INVALID MESSAGE LENGTH` against `BO`.\n- RSA-2048 with `CE1` accepts 245 bytes, or 490 hexadecimal characters. A 246-byte value returns `AM13`.\n- Do not use GPEA to encrypt an asymmetric private-key block directly. Encrypt the block with a symmetric key, then wrap that symmetric key with the recipient’s RSA public key.",
      "en": "GPEA encrypts the hexadecimal plaintext in `BO` with the RSA public key in `RC`. The `2-6144` range is the protocol field limit, not the RSA plaintext capacity. `CE1` (PKCS #1 v1.5, default) allows at most `k - 11` plaintext bytes, where `k` is the RSA modulus length in bytes. `CE4` (OAEP) allows at most `k - (2 × hLen) - 2` bytes, where `hLen` is the selected hash length. `CE0` requires plaintext exactly as long as the modulus.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- `BO` must contain an even number of hexadecimal characters. Odd-length values return `AM13 INVALID MESSAGE LENGTH` against `BO`.\n- RSA-2048 with `CE1` accepts 245 bytes, or 490 hexadecimal characters. A 246-byte value returns `AM13`.\n- Do not use GPEA to encrypt an asymmetric private-key block directly. Encrypt the block with a symmetric key, then wrap that symmetric key with the recipient’s RSA public key."
    },
