    "id": "futurex-gpin-req_319",
    "code": "GPIN",
    "direction": "request",
    "pairedCode": "GPIN",
    "name": {
      "es": "GPIN: Diebold",
      "en": "GPIN: Diebold"
    },
    "summary": {
      "es": "This command generates a random PIN and calculates the offset for the PIN by using the Diebold PIN creation method. The response returns the offset value and the PIN (an ANSI-format encrypted PIN block). The ANSI PIN block is encrypted under the PEK. This method can also return the natural PIN with an offset equal to zero.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS mode",
      "en": "This command generates a random PIN and calculates the offset for the PIN by using the Diebold PIN creation method. The response returns the offset value and the PIN (an ANSI-format encrypted PIN block). The ANSI PIN block is encrypted under the PEK. This method can also return the natural PIN with an offset equal to zero.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS mode"
    },
    "description": {
      "es": "This command generates a random PIN and calculates the offset for the PIN by using the Diebold PIN creation method. The response returns the offset value and the PIN (an ANSI-format encrypted PIN block). The ANSI PIN block is encrypted under the PEK. This method can also return the natural PIN with an offset equal to zero.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS mode",
      "en": "This command generates a random PIN and calculates the offset for the PIN by using the Diebold PIN creation method. The response returns the offset value and the PIN (an ANSI-format encrypted PIN block). The ANSI PIN block is encrypted under the PEK. This method can also return the natural PIN with an offset equal to zero.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS mode"
    },
