    "summary": {
      "es": "This command returns the version number, total user key slots, and key counts.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- By default, this command returns the number of available keys based on total available key slots, total user key slots, and available data space.\n- If only the command indicator token is passed, all tokens available display in the response.\n- If you request individual parameter tokens, the response includes only those parameters.\n- If requested, this command also returns the number of used key slots by type.",
      "en": "This command returns the version number, total user key slots, and key counts.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- By default, this command returns the number of available keys based on total available key slots, total user key slots, and available data space.\n- If only the command indicator token is passed, all tokens available display in the response.\n- If you request individual parameter tokens, the response includes only those parameters.\n- If requested, this command also returns the number of used key slots by type."
    },
    "description": {
      "es": "This command returns the version number, total user key slots, and key counts.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- By default, this command returns the number of available keys based on total available key slots, total user key slots, and available data space.\n- If only the command indicator token is passed, all tokens available display in the response.\n- If you request individual parameter tokens, the response includes only those parameters.\n- If requested, this command also returns the number of used key slots by type.",
      "en": "This command returns the version number, total user key slots, and key counts.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- By default, this command returns the number of available keys based on total available key slots, total user key slots, and available data space.\n- If only the command indicator token is passed, all tokens available display in the response.\n- If you request individual parameter tokens, the response includes only those parameters.\n- If requested, this command also returns the number of used key slots by type."
    },
