      "es": "# GPRW: General Purpose Key Wrap (with RSA)\n\nFuente: [GPRW: General Purpose Key Wrap (with RSA)](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/wrap/gprw-general-purpose-key-wrap-with-rsa)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:04:27.346Z\n\n---\n\nThis command wraps a symmetric key with an RSA public key.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This command is part of the **GPKW** family. To view more information about how this command works with other commands in the **GPKW** family, see the **GPKW Family** resource.\n- This command requires two users to log into the HSM before sending requests.\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| General Purpose | Enabled by default on all Vectera Series HSMs and available as an add-on license for Excrypt Series HSMs. |\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Keys | View key and table information | Mgmt | 0 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `RC` | Public key to wrap with (asymmetric) (KEK) under modifier 1 of major key | Hexadecimal | 16-4096 | Yes |\n| `BG` | Key to be wrapped (symmetric) under major key modifier AS | Hexadecimal | <br><br>16<br><br>32<br><br>48<br><br>74<br><br>88<br><br> | Yes |\n| `AS` | Modifier of major key that BG is under | Hexadecimal | 1-2 | Optional |\n| `FS` | Major key that BG or RC is under | Numeric | 1 | Optional |\n| `CE` | Padding | Numeric | 1 | Optional |\n| `OP` | Hashing algorithm used in OAEP (if using OAEP padding) | Numeric | 1 | Optional |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `BG` | Cryptogram of BG under RC | Hexadecimal | 16-4096 |\n| `AE` | Checksum of clear key | Hexadecimal | 4-8 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `GPRW` |\n\n<a id=\"rc-public-key-to-wrap-with-asymmetric-kek-under-modifier-1-of-major-key\"></a>\n\n### RC - Public Key to wrap with (asymmetric) (KEK) under modifier 1 of major key\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16-4096 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"bg-key-to-be-wrapped-symmetric-under-major-key-modifier-as\"></a>\n\n### BG - Key to be wrapped (symmetric) under major key modifier AS\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16<br>32<br>48<br>74<br>88 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"optional-as-modifier-of-major-key-that-bg-is-under\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) AS - Modifier of major key that BG is under\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-2 | Hexadecimal | `0`: Key Encryption Key (KEK) (default)<br>`2`: Data Encryption Key (DEK)<br>`3`: Message Authentication Key (MAK)<br>`8`: Base Derivation Key (BDK)<br>`E`: Detachment Derivation Key |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-major-key-that-bg-or-rc-is-under\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - Major key that BG or RC is under\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: MFK<br>`6`: PMK (Default)<br>`7`: FTK (if PKCS11 is available) |\n\n<a id=\"optional-ce-padding\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) CE - Padding\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `0`: None<br>`1`: PKCS #1.5 (default)<br>`2`: Bit<br>`3`: Zero<br>`4`: OAEP |\n\n<a id=\"optional-op-hashing-algorithm-used-in-oaep-if-using-oaep-padding\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) OP - Hashing Algorithm used in OAEP (if using OAEP padding)\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: SHA-1 (default)<br>`4`: SHA-256<br>`6`: SHA-512 |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `GPRW` |\n\n<a id=\"bg-cryptogram-of-bg-under-rc\"></a>\n\n### BG - Cryptogram of BG under RC\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16-4096 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"ae-checksum-of-clear-key\"></a>\n\n### AE - Checksum of clear key\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4-8 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"command-example\"></a>\n\n## Command Example\n\n```\nRequest: [AOGPRW;;BGB195D27A8F486EAA0F39CDEC684B8FDDA667AE04CB0660E3E4A2EB0EEC207BAF440B131F998D182C;AS2;]\n\nResponse: [AOGPRW;AE48EC;;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"test-key-used\"></a>\n\n### Test Key Used\n\nPMK Test Key: 8888888888888888 AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF 1111111111111111 Check Digit: (financial 1E26) (cmac 3B5E)\n",
