      "en": "This command encrypts any number of bytes using subsequent requests.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- If padding is disabled, the total number of bytes sent must be a multiple of the cipher block size on the final call. Otherwise, an error occurs. If you enable padding, this does not apply, and the result is padded to the block size on the final call.\n- By default, the maximum length of an Excrypt request message is 15,360 characters. In firmware versions supporting a configurable max request message length, you can configure the limit through the Web Portal or Excrypt Manager.\n- There are two sets of request tokens - **Initial**and **Subsequent**."
