      "es": "# GPUB: General Purpose Key Unwrap with Key Strength Bypass\n\nFuente: [GPUB: General Purpose Key Unwrap with Key Strength Bypass](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/unwrap/gpub-general-purpose-key-unwrap-with-key-strength-bypass)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:04:30.976Z\n\n---\n\nThis command converts a key under a Key Encryption Key (modifier 0) to under a major key (any modifier). Allows unwrap with a weak KEK.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- Key Strength Bypass license is enabled in PCI HSM mode to only allow AES128 keys to be protected by RSA2048 keys.\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| General Purpose | Enabled by default on all Vectera Series HSMs and available as an add-on license for Excrypt Series HSMs. |\n| Key Strength Bypass | Enables you to protect a stronger key with a weaker key. |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `GPUB` |\n\n<a id=\"select-either-symmetric-key-or-private-asymmetric-key\"></a>\n\n### Select either symmetric key or Private asymmetric key\n\n<a id=\"symmetric-key\"></a>\n\n## Symmetric key\n\n<a id=\"ak-key-to-unwrap-with-symmetric-kek-under-modifier-0-of-major-key\"></a>\n\n### AK - Key to unwrap with (symmetric) (KEK) under modifier 0 of major key\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16-64 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"private-asymmetric-key\"></a>\n\n## Private asymmetric key\n\n<a id=\"rc-private-key-to-unwrap-with-asymmetric-kek-under-modifier-0-of-major-key\"></a>\n\n### RC - Private key to unwrap with (asymmetric) (KEK) under modifier 0 of major key\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16-4096 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"bg-key-to-be-unwrapped-under-modifier-0-of-the-kek\"></a>\n\n### BG - Key to be unwrapped. under modifier 0 of the KEK\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16-4096 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"optional-as-modifier-of-major-key-that-bg-will-output-under\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) AS - Modifier of major key that BG will output under\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-2 | Hexadecimal | `0`: Key Encryption Key (KEK) (default)<br>`2`: Data Encryption Key (DEK)<br>`3`: Message Authentication Key (MAK)<br>`8`: Base Derivation Key (BDK)<br>`E`: Detachment Derivation Key |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-major-key-that-ak-is-under-and-bg-will-be-under\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - Major key that AK is under and BG will be under\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: MFK<br>`6`: PMK (Default)<br>`7`: FTK (if PKCS11 is available) |\n\n<a id=\"optional-bj-symmetric-cipher-type\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) BJ - Symmetric Cipher Type\n\nDefault: ECB for DES, X9.102 for AES\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-2 | Numeric | `0`: ECB<br>`1`: CBC<br>`2`: CFB<br>`3`: CFB-1<br>`4`: CFB-8<br>`5`: CFB-64<br>`6`: CFB-128<br>`7`: OFB<br>`8`: CTR<br>`10`: AES KWP |\n\n<a id=\"optional-gh-initialization-vector-iv-if-applicable\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) GH - Initialization vector (IV) (if applicable)\n\nDefault: All 0s\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16<br>32 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"optional-za-is-iv-encrypted-under-major-key\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) ZA - Is IV encrypted under major key\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `0`: Encrypted (default)<br>`1`: Clear |\n\n<a id=\"optional-ce-padding\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) CE - Padding\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `0`: None<br>`1`: PKCS #1.5 (default)<br>`2`: Bit<br>`3`: Zero<br>`4`: OAEP |\n\n<a id=\"optional-op-hashing-algorithm-used-in-oaep-if-using-oaep-padding\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) OP - Hashing Algorithm used in OAEP (if using OAEP padding)\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: SHA-1<br>`4`: SHA-256<br>`6`: SHA-512 |\n\n<a id=\"optional-ct-key-type\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) CT - Key type\n\nNot needed if cipher = AES X9.102\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `0`: Empty<br>`1`: DES-1<br>`2`: DES-2<br>`3`: DES-3<br>`4`: AES-128<br>`5`: AES-192<br>`6`: AES-256<br>`8`: RSA-512<br>`9`: RSA-1024<br>`10`: RSA-2048<br>`11`: RSA-3072<br>`12`: RSA-4096 |\n\n<a id=\"optional-bd-key-slot-to-store-under\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) BD - Key slot to store under\n\nDefault: Return cryptogram\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-5 | Alphanumeric | 0 - 26000<br>`FIRST` |\n\n<a id=\"optional-cz-key-usage-for-unwrapped-key\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) CZ - Key usage for unwrapped key\n\nIf X9.102, this must be compatible with the key block header.\n\nDefault: Modifier dependent\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Alphanumeric | `B`: Encrypt & Decrypt<br>`E`: Encrypt<br>`D`: Decrypt<br>`C`: Generate & Verify MAC<br>`G`: Generate MAC / Sign-only<br>`V`: Verify MAC / Verify-only<br>`X`: Derive<br>`S`: Asymmetric Sign & Verify<br>`1`: Asymmetric Wrap<br>`2`: Asymmetric Unwrap<br>`3`: Asymmetric Wrap & Unwrap |\n\n<a id=\"optional-sf-security-usage-flags-for-unwrapped-key\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) SF - Security usage flags for unwrapped key\n\nIf X9.102, it must be compatible with the key block header.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `0`: None (default)<br>`1`: Private<br>`2`: Sensitive<br>`4`: Immutable |\n\n<a id=\"optional-cy-multi-key-usage-for-unwrapped-key-asymmetric-only\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) CY - Multi-key usage for unwrapped key (asymmetric only)\n\nOnly if you do not send token **CZ**.\n\nDefault: Sign/verify (SV)\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-7 | Alphabetic | `D`: Decrypt<br>`E`: Encrypt<br>`W`: Wrap<br>`U`: Unwrap<br>`S`: Sign<br>`V`: Verify<br>`X`: Derive |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `GPUB` |\n\n<a id=\"bg-cryptogram-of-bg-under-major-key-mod-as\"></a>\n\n### BG - Cryptogram of BG under Major key mod AS\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16-4096 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"ae-checksum-of-clear-key\"></a>\n\n### AE - Checksum of clear key\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4-8 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"bd-key-table-slot-if-bd-specified\"></a>\n\n### BD - Key table slot (if BD specified)\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-5 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"command-example\"></a>\n\n## Command Example\n\n```\nRequest: [AOGPUB;AKC81FA4C01612979AA7645835B9FF1BC19F14138187E58841087C73127CBD5A2BA1830B53AB874773120059839CF65837;CT12;;]\n\nResponse: [AOGPUB;AE00A9;;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"test-key-used\"></a>\n\n### Test Key Used\n\nPMK Test Key: 8888888888888888 AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF 1111111111111111 Check Digit: (financial 1E26) (cmac 3B5E)\n",
