    "id": "futurex-grsa-req",
    "code": "GRSA",
    "direction": "request",
    "pairedCode": "GRSA",
    "name": {
      "es": "GRSA: Generate RSA Key",
      "en": "GRSA: Generate RSA Key"
    },
    "summary": {
      "es": "This command generates RSA Private and Public keys, both encrypted under a major key.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- If RSA Legacy mode is not enabled, the response does not include the trusted public key (token **SD** ).\n- While the API recognizes PKI storage to be slots 0-99, the Excrypt Manager loads keys into slots 1-100. Therefore, for tokens that support PKI storage table indexing, the key slot in which the key is loaded using Excrypt Manager is off by one (for example, a key loaded into slot **1** on the Excrypt Manager is referenced in the API as slot **0**).\n- If autonomous signing is turned off, this command outputs encrypted public keys.\n- Generation time scales with `RB`. Typical wall-clock for a single GRSA call ranges from roughly 5 seconds at smaller modulus sizes to ~20 seconds for `RB8192` (the largest supported value); plan client timeouts accordingly.\n- GRSA serializes key-pair generation. While one call is still running, a concurrent GRSA request returns `AM56 KEY GENERATION IN PROGRESS` with `AN` set to `GRSA` (the command name, not a token name) and no result tokens. Wait for the prior call to complete before retrying.",
      "en": "This command generates RSA Private and Public keys, both encrypted under a major key.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- If RSA Legacy mode is not enabled, the response does not include the trusted public key (token **SD** ).\n- While the API recognizes PKI storage to be slots 0-99, the Excrypt Manager loads keys into slots 1-100. Therefore, for tokens that support PKI storage table indexing, the key slot in which the key is loaded using Excrypt Manager is off by one (for example, a key loaded into slot **1** on the Excrypt Manager is referenced in the API as slot **0**).\n- If autonomous signing is turned off, this command outputs encrypted public keys.\n- Generation time scales with `RB`. Typical wall-clock for a single GRSA call ranges from roughly 5 seconds at smaller modulus sizes to ~20 seconds for `RB8192` (the largest supported value); plan client timeouts accordingly.\n- GRSA serializes key-pair generation. While one call is still running, a concurrent GRSA request returns `AM56 KEY GENERATION IN PROGRESS` with `AN` set to `GRSA` (the command name, not a token name) and no result tokens. Wait for the prior call to complete before retrying."
    },
    "description": {
      "es": "This command generates RSA Private and Public keys, both encrypted under a major key.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- If RSA Legacy mode is not enabled, the response does not include the trusted public key (token **SD** ).\n- While the API recognizes PKI storage to be slots 0-99, the Excrypt Manager loads keys into slots 1-100. Therefore, for tokens that support PKI storage table indexing, the key slot in which the key is loaded using Excrypt Manager is off by one (for example, a key loaded into slot **1** on the Excrypt Manager is referenced in the API as slot **0**).\n- If autonomous signing is turned off, this command outputs encrypted public keys.\n- Generation time scales with `RB`. Typical wall-clock for a single GRSA call ranges from roughly 5 seconds at smaller modulus sizes to ~20 seconds for `RB8192` (the largest supported value); plan client timeouts accordingly.\n- GRSA serializes key-pair generation. While one call is still running, a concurrent GRSA request returns `AM56 KEY GENERATION IN PROGRESS` with `AN` set to `GRSA` (the command name, not a token name) and no result tokens. Wait for the prior call to complete before retrying.",
      "en": "This command generates RSA Private and Public keys, both encrypted under a major key.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- If RSA Legacy mode is not enabled, the response does not include the trusted public key (token **SD** ).\n- While the API recognizes PKI storage to be slots 0-99, the Excrypt Manager loads keys into slots 1-100. Therefore, for tokens that support PKI storage table indexing, the key slot in which the key is loaded using Excrypt Manager is off by one (for example, a key loaded into slot **1** on the Excrypt Manager is referenced in the API as slot **0**).\n- If autonomous signing is turned off, this command outputs encrypted public keys.\n- Generation time scales with `RB`. Typical wall-clock for a single GRSA call ranges from roughly 5 seconds at smaller modulus sizes to ~20 seconds for `RB8192` (the largest supported value); plan client timeouts accordingly.\n- GRSA serializes key-pair generation. While one call is still running, a concurrent GRSA request returns `AM56 KEY GENERATION IN PROGRESS` with `AN` set to `GRSA` (the command name, not a token name) and no result tokens. Wait for the prior call to complete before retrying."
    },
