      "en": "This command generates a random DES key for use in the VISA network.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This command generates odd parity keys only.\n- Notes about TR-31 headers:  \n\n  - If no header is sent in but a TR-31 key block is requested (OF token), then it defaults to B mode of use, P0 key usage, and B TR-31 mode.\n  - If a header is sent in the AK token, both keys in the response use this header.\n  - If headers are sent in the AK and AV tokens, then the key under the MFK uses the header in the AK token, and the key under the ZCMK uses the header in the AV token."
