    "id": "futurex-hash-req",
    "code": "HASH",
    "direction": "request",
    "pairedCode": "HASH",
    "name": {
      "es": "HASH: Return Serial Number",
      "en": "HASH: Return Serial Number"
    },
    "summary": {
      "es": "This command returns a value delineating the unit internal serial number.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The serial number returned is different from the manufacturing serial number physically listed on the back or top of the HSM. It matches the number that shows up on the HSM LCD panel.\n- When sent on port 9000, the command returns the serial number of the HSM by default.\n- When sent on port 9010, the command returns the serial number of the HSM as seven hexadecimal values separated with commas. In addition, the command returns the number of Admin users on the card.\n- When sent on a virtual HSM, the command returns the serial number of the host HSM if configured to share.",
      "en": "This command returns a value delineating the unit internal serial number.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The serial number returned is different from the manufacturing serial number physically listed on the back or top of the HSM. It matches the number that shows up on the HSM LCD panel.\n- When sent on port 9000, the command returns the serial number of the HSM by default.\n- When sent on port 9010, the command returns the serial number of the HSM as seven hexadecimal values separated with commas. In addition, the command returns the number of Admin users on the card.\n- When sent on a virtual HSM, the command returns the serial number of the host HSM if configured to share."
    },
    "description": {
      "es": "This command returns a value delineating the unit internal serial number.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The serial number returned is different from the manufacturing serial number physically listed on the back or top of the HSM. It matches the number that shows up on the HSM LCD panel.\n- When sent on port 9000, the command returns the serial number of the HSM by default.\n- When sent on port 9010, the command returns the serial number of the HSM as seven hexadecimal values separated with commas. In addition, the command returns the number of Admin users on the card.\n- When sent on a virtual HSM, the command returns the serial number of the host HSM if configured to share.",
      "en": "This command returns a value delineating the unit internal serial number.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The serial number returned is different from the manufacturing serial number physically listed on the back or top of the HSM. It matches the number that shows up on the HSM LCD panel.\n- When sent on port 9000, the command returns the serial number of the HSM by default.\n- When sent on port 9010, the command returns the serial number of the HSM as seven hexadecimal values separated with commas. In addition, the command returns the number of Admin users on the card.\n- When sent on a virtual HSM, the command returns the serial number of the host HSM if configured to share."
    },
