    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# HENC: Encrypt Hash\n\nFuente: [HENC: Encrypt Hash](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/system/utility/henc-encrypt-hash)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:04:50.681Z\n\n---\n\nThis command accepts a clear message digest and encrypt it under modifier 30 of the MFK.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- Depending on the value used in token **BF**, this command takes different sections of the input data and outputs the result of the encryption in response token **AK**.  \n\n  - If the Hash type is `2` and the encoding method is `0` or `1`, the hash value must be 32 digits.\n  - If the Hash type is `3` and the encoding method is `0`, the hash value must be 40 digits even though only the left 32 digits are going to be used.\n  - If the Hash type is `3` and the encoding method is `1`, the hash value must be 70 digits even though only digits 30-62 are going to be used.\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `HENC` |\n\n<a id=\"ak-hash-value\"></a>\n\n### AK - Hash Value\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 32<br>40<br>70 | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"bf-hash-type\"></a>\n\n### BF - Hash Type\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `2`: MD5 (Hash value length must be 32 digits.)<br>`3`: SHA-1 (Hash value length must be 40 digits when the encoding method (token **FS**) is `0`, and 70 digits when the encoding method (token **FS**) is `1`.) |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-encoding\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - Encoding\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `0`: No encoding<br>`1`: Encoded hash |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `HENC` |\n\n<a id=\"ak-encrypted-hash-value\"></a>\n\n### AK - Encrypted Hash Value\n\nThis field is the first eight bytes of the Hash value encrypted under modifier 30 of the MFK.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16 | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"md5-hash-type-with-no-encoding\"></a>\n\n### MD5 Hash type with no encoding\n\n```\nRequest: [AOHENC;AK11112222333344445555666677778888;BF2;FS0;]\n\nResponse: [AOHENC;AKA515BBF1B701A7DB96A4F74BC856F87\n```\n\n<a id=\"encoded-md5-hash-type\"></a>\n\n### Encoded MD5 Hash type\n\n```\nRequest: [AOHENC;AK11112222333344445555666677778888;BF2;FS1;]\n\nResponse: [AOHENC;AK244ACABB167E884B2EEECC96A78A83CD;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"sha-1-hash-type-with-no-encoding\"></a>\n\n### SHA-1 Hash type with no encoding\n\n```\nRequest: [AOHENC;AK1111222233334444555566667777888812345678;BF3;FS0;]\n\nResponse: [AOHENC;AK244ACABB167E884B2EEECC96A78A83CD;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"encoded-sha-1-hash-type\"></a>\n\n### Encoded SHA-1 Hash type\n\n```\nRequest: [AOHENC;AK1111222233334444555566667777888812345678111112222233333444445555566666;BF3;FS1;]\n\nResponse: [AOHENC;AK79DE29270FC900EDE08FD3D82E708568;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"encoded-sha-1-hash-type-with-40-digit-length\"></a>\n\n### Encoded SHA-1 Hash type with 40 digit length\n\n```\nRequest: [AOHENC;AK1111222233334444555566667777888812345678;BF3;FS1;]\n\nResponse: [AOERRO;AM13;ANAK;BBINVALID MESSAGE LENGTH;]\n```\n",
      "en": "# HENC: Encrypt Hash\n\nFuente: [HENC: Encrypt Hash](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/system/utility/henc-encrypt-hash)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:04:50.681Z\n\n---\n\nThis command accepts a clear message digest and encrypt it under modifier 30 of the MFK.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- Depending on the value used in token **BF**, this command takes different sections of the input data and outputs the result of the encryption in response token **AK**.  \n\n  - If the Hash type is `2` and the encoding method is `0` or `1`, the hash value must be 32 digits.\n  - If the Hash type is `3` and the encoding method is `0`, the hash value must be 40 digits even though only the left 32 digits are going to be used.\n  - If the Hash type is `3` and the encoding method is `1`, the hash value must be 70 digits even though only digits 30-62 are going to be used.\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `HENC` |\n\n<a id=\"ak-hash-value\"></a>\n\n### AK - Hash Value\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 32<br>40<br>70 | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"bf-hash-type\"></a>\n\n### BF - Hash Type\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `2`: MD5 (Hash value length must be 32 digits.)<br>`3`: SHA-1 (Hash value length must be 40 digits when the encoding method (token **FS**) is `0`, and 70 digits when the encoding method (token **FS**) is `1`.) |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-encoding\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - Encoding\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `0`: No encoding<br>`1`: Encoded hash |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `HENC` |\n\n<a id=\"ak-encrypted-hash-value\"></a>\n\n### AK - Encrypted Hash Value\n\nThis field is the first eight bytes of the Hash value encrypted under modifier 30 of the MFK.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16 | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"md5-hash-type-with-no-encoding\"></a>\n\n### MD5 Hash type with no encoding\n\n```\nRequest: [AOHENC;AK11112222333344445555666677778888;BF2;FS0;]\n\nResponse: [AOHENC;AKA515BBF1B701A7DB96A4F74BC856F87\n```\n\n<a id=\"encoded-md5-hash-type\"></a>\n\n### Encoded MD5 Hash type\n\n```\nRequest: [AOHENC;AK11112222333344445555666677778888;BF2;FS1;]\n\nResponse: [AOHENC;AK244ACABB167E884B2EEECC96A78A83CD;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"sha-1-hash-type-with-no-encoding\"></a>\n\n### SHA-1 Hash type with no encoding\n\n```\nRequest: [AOHENC;AK1111222233334444555566667777888812345678;BF3;FS0;]\n\nResponse: [AOHENC;AK244ACABB167E884B2EEECC96A78A83CD;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"encoded-sha-1-hash-type\"></a>\n\n### Encoded SHA-1 Hash type\n\n```\nRequest: [AOHENC;AK1111222233334444555566667777888812345678111112222233333444445555566666;BF3;FS1;]\n\nResponse: [AOHENC;AK79DE29270FC900EDE08FD3D82E708568;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"encoded-sha-1-hash-type-with-40-digit-length\"></a>\n\n### Encoded SHA-1 Hash type with 40 digit length\n\n```\nRequest: [AOHENC;AK1111222233334444555566667777888812345678;BF3;FS1;]\n\nResponse: [AOERRO;AM13;ANAK;BBINVALID MESSAGE LENGTH;]\n```\n"
    }
