      "es": "# HEXE: Encode ASCII Data to Hex\n\nFuente: [HEXE: Encode ASCII Data to Hex](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/system/utility/hexe-encode-ascii-data-to-hex)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:04:46.072Z\n\n---\n\nThis command encodes ASCII data to hexadecimal for use in the firmware.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `AK` | Data | ASCII | 1-128 | Yes |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `AK` | Hex-encoded ASCII data | Hexadecimal | 2-256 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `HEXE` |\n\n<a id=\"ak-data\"></a>\n\n### AK - Data\n\nThis field is any ASCII value between **0x20** and **0x7E**, not including **[**, **]**, **<**, **>**, and **;** characters.\n\nAn error returns if you use any excluded characters.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-128 | ASCII | A-Z, a-z, 0-9 except [ ] <>; |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id-2\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `HEXE` |\n\n<a id=\"ak-hex-encoded-ascii-data\"></a>\n\n### AK - Hex-encoded ASCII data\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2-256 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n",
