      "en": "The IDEN command provides full lifecycle management for HSM identities. Use it to create new identities with passwords, PKI authentication certificates, and role assignments; modify existing identity attributes such as lock state, roles, or dual-factor public keys; retrieve detailed information about a specific identity or list all identities on the device; or delete identities that are no longer needed. When multiple PKI authentication certificates are loaded for an identity, the `get` operation in `general` mode returns `Multiple CAs Loaded` in the CE token; use `pki_auth_ca` mode to retrieve individual certificates by serial number. Identity operations that change configuration (add, modify, delete) require dual-control login on the management port.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- When in PCI HSM mode, the dual-factor public key in token PU must have a minimum size of RSA 2048 or ECC 224.\n- When in PCI HSM mode, the identity CA in token CE must have a minimum size of RSA 2048 or ECC 224.\n- An identity can have a maximum of 10 PKI authentication certificates, and their serial numbers must be unique.\n- Token CN always appends the given certificate to the identity and is processed after token CE."
