    "summary": {
      "es": "This command generates a bitmap representation of all the slots within the key table.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The resulting bitmap is an array of variable lengths corresponding to the number of slots within the key table.\n- Each hexadecimal character has four bits within it, with each bit representing one slot in the key table.\n- Can produce three different maps: one each for symmetric slots, asymmetric slots, and Diebold tables, along with corresponding slot totals.\n- The bare form `[AOKMAP;]` fails transport when the combined response exceeds the HSM’s **Max Request Message Length** setting (default 15360 bytes). Either supply **AK** to scope the query or raise the setting on the HSM (for instance to 65644 bytes).",
      "en": "This command generates a bitmap representation of all the slots within the key table.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The resulting bitmap is an array of variable lengths corresponding to the number of slots within the key table.\n- Each hexadecimal character has four bits within it, with each bit representing one slot in the key table.\n- Can produce three different maps: one each for symmetric slots, asymmetric slots, and Diebold tables, along with corresponding slot totals.\n- The bare form `[AOKMAP;]` fails transport when the combined response exceeds the HSM’s **Max Request Message Length** setting (default 15360 bytes). Either supply **AK** to scope the query or raise the setting on the HSM (for instance to 65644 bytes)."
    },
