    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# LCDT: Load Clear Diebold Table\n\nFuente: [LCDT: Load Clear Diebold Table](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/key_tables/lcdt-load-clear-diebold-table)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:07:39.447Z\n\n---\n\nThis command loads an unencrypted Diebold table into the Diebold storage table in the HSM.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- Excrypt does not prevent users from writing over existing data in the storage table. Users should assign locations carefully.\n- The table is sent as 512 bytes of hexadecimal ASCII text.\n- The Diebold storage table shares the same space as the key storage table. For systems that are not also storing DES keys, there is room to store 125 Diebold tables.\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permissions | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Keys | View key and table information | Mgmt | 0 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `BR` | Diebold table index number | Numeric | 1-3 | Yes |\n| `BO` | Diebold number table (clear) | Hexadecimal | 512 | Yes |\n| `IA` | Diebold table indexing format | Numeric | 1 | Optional |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `BR` | Loaded Diebold table index number | Numeric | 1-3 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `LCDT` |\n\n<a id=\"br-diebold-table-index-number\"></a>\n\n### BR - Diebold table index number\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-3 | Numeric | 0 - 124 |\n\n<a id=\"bo-diebold-number-table-clear\"></a>\n\n### BO - Diebold number table (clear)\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 512 | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"optional-ia-diebold-table-indexing-format\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) IA - Diebold table indexing format\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `0`: Use Excrypt API Diebold table indexing (default)<br>`1`: Use Standard API Diebold table indexing |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `LCDT` |\n\n<a id=\"br-loaded-diebold-table-index-number\"></a>\n\n### BR - Loaded Diebold table index number\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-3 | Numeric | 0 - 124 |\n\n<a id=\"command-example\"></a>\n\n## Command example\n\n```\nRequest: [AOLCDT;BR0;;]\n\nResponse: [AOLCDT;BR0;]\n```\n",
      "en": "# LCDT: Load Clear Diebold Table\n\nFuente: [LCDT: Load Clear Diebold Table](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/key_tables/lcdt-load-clear-diebold-table)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:07:39.447Z\n\n---\n\nThis command loads an unencrypted Diebold table into the Diebold storage table in the HSM.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- Excrypt does not prevent users from writing over existing data in the storage table. Users should assign locations carefully.\n- The table is sent as 512 bytes of hexadecimal ASCII text.\n- The Diebold storage table shares the same space as the key storage table. For systems that are not also storing DES keys, there is room to store 125 Diebold tables.\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permissions | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Keys | View key and table information | Mgmt | 0 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `BR` | Diebold table index number | Numeric | 1-3 | Yes |\n| `BO` | Diebold number table (clear) | Hexadecimal | 512 | Yes |\n| `IA` | Diebold table indexing format | Numeric | 1 | Optional |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `BR` | Loaded Diebold table index number | Numeric | 1-3 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `LCDT` |\n\n<a id=\"br-diebold-table-index-number\"></a>\n\n### BR - Diebold table index number\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-3 | Numeric | 0 - 124 |\n\n<a id=\"bo-diebold-number-table-clear\"></a>\n\n### BO - Diebold number table (clear)\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 512 | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"optional-ia-diebold-table-indexing-format\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) IA - Diebold table indexing format\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `0`: Use Excrypt API Diebold table indexing (default)<br>`1`: Use Standard API Diebold table indexing |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `LCDT` |\n\n<a id=\"br-loaded-diebold-table-index-number\"></a>\n\n### BR - Loaded Diebold table index number\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-3 | Numeric | 0 - 124 |\n\n<a id=\"command-example\"></a>\n\n## Command example\n\n```\nRequest: [AOLCDT;BR0;;]\n\nResponse: [AOLCDT;BR0;]\n```\n"
    }
