      "en": "LKEY loads a clear-text key component into the HSM working buffer. Components are loaded sequentially (`BJ1` through `BJ12`) and XORed together in the buffer to assemble a complete key. Sending `BJ0` retrieves the current check digit without modifying the buffer. If `AK` is omitted but `AS` specifies a key type, the HSM generates a random component of that type.\n\nUse LKEY in split-knowledge key ceremonies where each custodian enters one component. After all components are loaded, use a key-injection command to move the assembled key from the working buffer into a key slot.\n\n> **Warning:** Allows clear key components to be loaded into the working buffer. Any use of this command must be secured, and Futurex strongly discourages its use."
