    "name": {
      "es": "LKST: Load Key Storage Table",
      "en": "LKST: Load Key Storage Table"
    },
    "summary": {
      "es": "This command loads a key to a defined key storage table location. Using the Excrypt message interface, you can explicitly assign a key to a Key Storage Table location by using the **BD** token. This is especially useful when trying to synchronize the Key Storage Tables in a number of Excrypt boards. This method differs from the standard interface, which automatically assigns the key to a table location and then shows the location in the response message.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n> **Warning:** WARNING\n> \n> \n> \n> When you assign a key to a key storage table location, the key overwrites any other data already stored in that location.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- You can use Excrypt command [**VKTE: Verify Key Table Entry**](../key_tables/vkte-verify-key-table-entry.md) to examine the contents of a table location. The checksum for the key stored at the location is returned.\n- Token**AS** must precede token **BG** so the HSM knows what modifier to use to decrypt the working key.",
      "en": "This command loads a key to a defined key storage table location. Using the Excrypt message interface, you can explicitly assign a key to a Key Storage Table location by using the **BD** token. This is especially useful when trying to synchronize the Key Storage Tables in a number of Excrypt boards. This method differs from the standard interface, which automatically assigns the key to a table location and then shows the location in the response message.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n> **Warning:** WARNING\n> \n> \n> \n> When you assign a key to a key storage table location, the key overwrites any other data already stored in that location.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- You can use Excrypt command [**VKTE: Verify Key Table Entry**](../key_tables/vkte-verify-key-table-entry.md) to examine the contents of a table location. The checksum for the key stored at the location is returned.\n- Token**AS** must precede token **BG** so the HSM knows what modifier to use to decrypt the working key."
    },
    "description": {
      "es": "This command loads a key to a defined key storage table location. Using the Excrypt message interface, you can explicitly assign a key to a Key Storage Table location by using the **BD** token. This is especially useful when trying to synchronize the Key Storage Tables in a number of Excrypt boards. This method differs from the standard interface, which automatically assigns the key to a table location and then shows the location in the response message.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n> **Warning:** WARNING\n> \n> \n> \n> When you assign a key to a key storage table location, the key overwrites any other data already stored in that location.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- You can use Excrypt command [**VKTE: Verify Key Table Entry**](../key_tables/vkte-verify-key-table-entry.md) to examine the contents of a table location. The checksum for the key stored at the location is returned.\n- Token**AS** must precede token **BG** so the HSM knows what modifier to use to decrypt the working key.",
      "en": "This command loads a key to a defined key storage table location. Using the Excrypt message interface, you can explicitly assign a key to a Key Storage Table location by using the **BD** token. This is especially useful when trying to synchronize the Key Storage Tables in a number of Excrypt boards. This method differs from the standard interface, which automatically assigns the key to a table location and then shows the location in the response message.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n> **Warning:** WARNING\n> \n> \n> \n> When you assign a key to a key storage table location, the key overwrites any other data already stored in that location.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- You can use Excrypt command [**VKTE: Verify Key Table Entry**](../key_tables/vkte-verify-key-table-entry.md) to examine the contents of a table location. The checksum for the key stored at the location is returned.\n- Token**AS** must precede token **BG** so the HSM knows what modifier to use to decrypt the working key."
    },
