    "summary": {
      "es": "This command loads a key into the key table. You can also use this command to convert the RSA key usage in General Purpose (GP) mode.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- To load a public key, use the **SD** token, and to load a private key, use the **RC** token. If both are specified, the private key is used.\n- While the API recognizes PKI storage to be slots 0–99, the Excrypt Manager loads keys into slots 1–100. Therefore, for tokens that support PKI storage table indexing, the key slot in which the key is loaded using Excrypt Manager is off by one (for example, a key loaded into slot **1** on the Excrypt Manager is referenced in the API as slot **0**).\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode",
      "en": "This command loads a key into the key table. You can also use this command to convert the RSA key usage in General Purpose (GP) mode.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- To load a public key, use the **SD** token, and to load a private key, use the **RC** token. If both are specified, the private key is used.\n- While the API recognizes PKI storage to be slots 0–99, the Excrypt Manager loads keys into slots 1–100. Therefore, for tokens that support PKI storage table indexing, the key slot in which the key is loaded using Excrypt Manager is off by one (for example, a key loaded into slot **1** on the Excrypt Manager is referenced in the API as slot **0**).\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode"
    },
