    "source": "Futurex Excrypt Command Reference Manual v7.6.1 (LVMQ)",
    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# LVMQ: List Active Memory Queue\n\nFuente: [LVMQ: List Active Memory Queue](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/system/admin/lvmq-list-view-active-memory-queue)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:07:44.203Z\n\n---\n\nLVMQ retrieves a summary of all active stateful memory queue sessions on the HSM. Each entry in the response identifies a memory queue type and how many sessions are currently active for that type. Use this command to monitor queue utilization or to identify stale sessions before clearing them with RMMQ.\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `OP` | Operation | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `DN` | Active queue list | ASCII | Variable |\n| `TM` | Total active sessions | Numeric | 1-5 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\nCommand ID for this request.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `LVMQ` |\n\n<a id=\"op-operation\"></a>\n\n### OP - Operation\n\nSpecifies the operation to perform.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `list`: List all active stateful memory queue sessions. |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id-2\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\nEchoes the command code from the request.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `LVMQ` |\n\n<a id=\"dn-active-queue-list\"></a>\n\n### DN - Active queue list\n\nList of memory queue types that have active memory queues, with the count for each type.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Variable | ASCII | Comma-separated list in the format `Name:Count` |\n\n<a id=\"tm-total-active-sessions\"></a>\n\n### TM - Total active sessions\n\nTotal number of active stateful memory queue sessions across all types.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-5 | Numeric | `0`-`50000` |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"list-all-active-memory-queues\"></a>\n\n### List all active memory queues\n\n```\nRequest: [AOLVMQ;OPlist;]\n\nResponse: [AOLVMQ;DNDUMP:4,GHSH:5,HMCX:5,KEYC:5,PGPD:5,PGPE:5,PING:5,PRSL:5,CSKL:5;]\n```\n",
      "en": "# LVMQ: List Active Memory Queue\n\nFuente: [LVMQ: List Active Memory Queue](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/system/admin/lvmq-list-view-active-memory-queue)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:07:44.203Z\n\n---\n\nLVMQ retrieves a summary of all active stateful memory queue sessions on the HSM. Each entry in the response identifies a memory queue type and how many sessions are currently active for that type. Use this command to monitor queue utilization or to identify stale sessions before clearing them with RMMQ.\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `OP` | Operation | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `DN` | Active queue list | ASCII | Variable |\n| `TM` | Total active sessions | Numeric | 1-5 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\nCommand ID for this request.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `LVMQ` |\n\n<a id=\"op-operation\"></a>\n\n### OP - Operation\n\nSpecifies the operation to perform.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `list`: List all active stateful memory queue sessions. |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id-2\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\nEchoes the command code from the request.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `LVMQ` |\n\n<a id=\"dn-active-queue-list\"></a>\n\n### DN - Active queue list\n\nList of memory queue types that have active memory queues, with the count for each type.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Variable | ASCII | Comma-separated list in the format `Name:Count` |\n\n<a id=\"tm-total-active-sessions\"></a>\n\n### TM - Total active sessions\n\nTotal number of active stateful memory queue sessions across all types.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-5 | Numeric | `0`-`50000` |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"list-all-active-memory-queues\"></a>\n\n### List all active memory queues\n\n```\nRequest: [AOLVMQ;OPlist;]\n\nResponse: [AOLVMQ;DNDUMP:4,GHSH:5,HMCX:5,KEYC:5,PGPD:5,PGPE:5,PING:5,PRSL:5,CSKL:5;]\n```\n"
    }
