      "en": "NTPD manages Network Time Protocol (NTP) server configuration on the HSM. The OP token selects the operation mode: add a new NTP server, modify or delete an existing one, show current configuration, or start, stop, and restart the NTP service. Each mode accepts a different combination of request tokens as described below.\n\nUse this command to keep the HSM clock synchronized with external time sources, which is important for accurate audit logs, certificate validity checks, and time-sensitive cryptographic operations."
