      "es": "# PKEY: Key Component Generator\n\nFuente: [PKEY: Key Component Generator](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/import/pkey-key-component-generator)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:07:58.098Z\n\n---\n\nThis command generates a set of key components, which you can use together to form a key.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permissions | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Keys | View key and table information | Mgmt | 0 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `PKEY` |\n\n<a id=\"gr-number-of-key-components\"></a>\n\n### GR - Number of key components\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | 1 - 9 |\n\n<a id=\"fs-key-length\"></a>\n\n### FS - Key length\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: 16<br>`2`: 32<br>`3`: 48 |\n\n<a id=\"ak-force-odd-key-parity\"></a>\n\n### AK - Force odd key parity\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `NONE`: No odd parity<br>`ODDC`: Force odd key parity |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `PKEY` |\n\n<a id=\"fs-key-length-2\"></a>\n\n### FS - Key length\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: 16<br>`2`: 32<br>`3`: 48 |\n\nGR - Number of key components\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | 1 - 9 |\n\n> **Note:** <a id=\"the-following-tokens-are-repeated-in-the-response-as-many-times-as-returned-in-token-gr\"></a>\n> \n> ### The following tokens are repeated in the response as many times as returned in token GR.\n\n<a id=\"w-x-key-part-x\"></a>\n\n#### W(X) - Key part (X)\n\nValue (X) begins with the letter A and increases by one letter for each key component returned.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16<br>32<br>48 | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"x-x-checksum-corresponding-to-key-part-x\"></a>\n\n#### X(X) - Checksum corresponding to key part (X)\n\nValue (X) begins with the letter A and increases by one letter for each key part checksum returned.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4-8 | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"xj-full-key-checksum\"></a>\n\n### XJ - Full key checksum\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4-8 | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"single-key-component-with-force-odd-parity\"></a>\n\n### Single Key Component with Force Odd Parity\n\n```\nRequest: [AOPKEY;GR1;FS1;AKODDC;]\n\nResponse: [AOPKEY;FS1;GR1;WAC26D343E37BF1AA2;XA70AF;XJ70AF;]\t&#x9;\n```\n\n<a id=\"three-key-components\"></a>\n\n### Three Key Components\n\n**Example 1 with Force Odd Parity**\n\n```\nRequest: [AOPKEY;GR3;FS2;AKODDC;]\n\nResponse: [AOPKEY;FS2;GR3;WABCB6580D9DC7BA58641573BA205D29B9;XAC86CB1B0;WBD53420B5B3E04C4A460BF483F83B9B6E;XBC0A627BE;WC835207E5CEFDEFE608B6DF8F4C161964;XC7E0D08F5;XJ99A3FE6E;]\n```\n\n**Example 2 with No Odd Parity**\n\n```\nRequest: [AOPKEY;GR3;FS2;AKNONE;]\n\nResponse: [AOPKEY;FS2;GR3;WA0F8C29F77D31BED1354D9D25B9796AAB;XA9BE292D9;WB68CBDEE1F2DD0A431A6A3757C767510D;XB44ED7197;WC2D84EDED1204574A6E4A9D7C1A93D37D;XC79612044;XJA24A13\n```\n",
      "en": "# PKEY: Key Component Generator\n\nFuente: [PKEY: Key Component Generator](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/import/pkey-key-component-generator)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:07:58.098Z\n\n---\n\nThis command generates a set of key components, which you can use together to form a key.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permissions | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Keys | View key and table information | Mgmt | 0 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `PKEY` |\n\n<a id=\"gr-number-of-key-components\"></a>\n\n### GR - Number of key components\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | 1 - 9 |\n\n<a id=\"fs-key-length\"></a>\n\n### FS - Key length\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: 16<br>`2`: 32<br>`3`: 48 |\n\n<a id=\"ak-force-odd-key-parity\"></a>\n\n### AK - Force odd key parity\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `NONE`: No odd parity<br>`ODDC`: Force odd key parity |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `PKEY` |\n\n<a id=\"fs-key-length-2\"></a>\n\n### FS - Key length\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: 16<br>`2`: 32<br>`3`: 48 |\n\nGR - Number of key components\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | 1 - 9 |\n\n> **Note:** <a id=\"the-following-tokens-are-repeated-in-the-response-as-many-times-as-returned-in-token-gr\"></a>\n> \n> ### The following tokens are repeated in the response as many times as returned in token GR.\n\n<a id=\"w-x-key-part-x\"></a>\n\n#### W(X) - Key part (X)\n\nValue (X) begins with the letter A and increases by one letter for each key component returned.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16<br>32<br>48 | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"x-x-checksum-corresponding-to-key-part-x\"></a>\n\n#### X(X) - Checksum corresponding to key part (X)\n\nValue (X) begins with the letter A and increases by one letter for each key part checksum returned.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4-8 | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"xj-full-key-checksum\"></a>\n\n### XJ - Full key checksum\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4-8 | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"single-key-component-with-force-odd-parity\"></a>\n\n### Single Key Component with Force Odd Parity\n\n```\nRequest: [AOPKEY;GR1;FS1;AKODDC;]\n\nResponse: [AOPKEY;FS1;GR1;WAC26D343E37BF1AA2;XA70AF;XJ70AF;]\t&#x9;\n```\n\n<a id=\"three-key-components\"></a>\n\n### Three Key Components\n\n**Example 1 with Force Odd Parity**\n\n```\nRequest: [AOPKEY;GR3;FS2;AKODDC;]\n\nResponse: [AOPKEY;FS2;GR3;WABCB6580D9DC7BA58641573BA205D29B9;XAC86CB1B0;WBD53420B5B3E04C4A460BF483F83B9B6E;XBC0A627BE;WC835207E5CEFDEFE608B6DF8F4C161964;XC7E0D08F5;XJ99A3FE6E;]\n```\n\n**Example 2 with No Odd Parity**\n\n```\nRequest: [AOPKEY;GR3;FS2;AKNONE;]\n\nResponse: [AOPKEY;FS2;GR3;WA0F8C29F77D31BED1354D9D25B9796AAB;XA9BE292D9;WB68CBDEE1F2DD0A431A6A3757C767510D;XB44ED7197;WC2D84EDED1204574A6E4A9D7C1A93D37D;XC79612044;XJA24A13\n```\n"
