      "en": "# PQCF: Derive a quantum-safe shared secret from a payload (General Purpose)\n\nFuente: [PQCF: Derive a quantum-safe shared secret from a payload (General Purpose)](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/asymmetric/derive_shared_secret/pqcf-derive-a-quantum-safe-shared-secret-from-a-payload-general-purpose)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:08:26.241Z\n\n---\n\nThis command uses a Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC) CRYSTALS-Kyber public key to derive a shared secret from a given payload.\n\n> **Warning:** Disabled in PCI HSM Mode Pending PCI Approval\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| Post Quantum Cryptography | Enables Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC) commands and functionality. |\n| Clear Shared Secret | Allows the HSM to support commands that will directly output the clear shared secret value.<br>`Required in FW 7.6.1.4 and later.` |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `PQCF` |\n\n<a id=\"rc-crystals-kyber-public-key\"></a>\n\n### RC - CRYSTALS-Kyber public key\n\n**Note**\n\n- Derive usage, PMK\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Variable | ASCII | A - Z, a - z, 0 - 9 except ; [ ] |\n\n<a id=\"bo-payload-from-peer\"></a>\n\n### BO - Payload from peer\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Variable | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Value |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `PQCF` |\n\n<a id=\"an-success-indicator\"></a>\n\n### AN - Success indicator\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Value |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Alphabetic | `Y` |\n\n<a id=\"ak-derived-secret\"></a>\n\n### AK - Derived secret\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Value |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Variable | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"command-example\"></a>\n\n## Command example\n\n```\nRequest: [AOPQCF;;;]\n\nResponse: [AOPQCF;ANY;AK3CA7F4996DD7D01DAA09CCD4E484E0AEE81441F6E399B4CB927DE95B422E210F;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"changelog\"></a>\n\n## Changelog\n\n2024-07-29\n\n- Added **FW-14861** | Require the Clear Shared Secret license.\n\n2024-07-03\n\n- Fixed **FW-14446** | Resolved an issue when attempting to use this command by the transaction processing role.\n- Added **FW-14246** | New Excrypt Command.\n"
