      "es": "# RAND: Generate Random Data\n\nFuente: [RAND: Generate Random Data](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/system/utility/rand-generate-random-data)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:08:28.250Z\n\n---\n\nThis command generates random data using a NIST SP 800-90A certified pseudorandom number generator.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Note**\n\n- The Max Return Size from HSM API is 16,384 bytes. This includes requested data as well as token tags and delimiters. Keep any added AG (context) tag to this command under 1,024 bytes.\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Management Commands:Crypto | Gives permission to perform basic crypto operations on the administrative port. | Mgmt | 1 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `AL` | Number of random bytes | Numeric | 1-4 | Yes |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `AK` | Hex encoded random output | Hexadecimal | 2-15360 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RAND` |\n\n<a id=\"al-number-of-random-bytes\"></a>\n\n### AL - Number of random bytes\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | 1 - 7680 |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RAND` |\n\n<a id=\"ak-hex-encoded-random-output\"></a>\n\n### AK - Hex encoded random output\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2-15360 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"one-byte-data\"></a>\n\n## One-Byte data\n\n```\nRequest: [AORAND;AL1;]\n\nResponse: [AORAND;AK61;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"10-byte-data\"></a>\n\n## 10-Byte data\n\n```\nRequest: [AORAND;AL10;]\n\nResponse: [AORAND;AKB00149DEF90ACE31C3DC;]\n```\n",
      "en": "# RAND: Generate Random Data\n\nFuente: [RAND: Generate Random Data](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/system/utility/rand-generate-random-data)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:08:28.250Z\n\n---\n\nThis command generates random data using a NIST SP 800-90A certified pseudorandom number generator.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Note**\n\n- The Max Return Size from HSM API is 16,384 bytes. This includes requested data as well as token tags and delimiters. Keep any added AG (context) tag to this command under 1,024 bytes.\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Management Commands:Crypto | Gives permission to perform basic crypto operations on the administrative port. | Mgmt | 1 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `AL` | Number of random bytes | Numeric | 1-4 | Yes |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `AK` | Hex encoded random output | Hexadecimal | 2-15360 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RAND` |\n\n<a id=\"al-number-of-random-bytes\"></a>\n\n### AL - Number of random bytes\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | 1 - 7680 |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RAND` |\n\n<a id=\"ak-hex-encoded-random-output\"></a>\n\n### AK - Hex encoded random output\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2-15360 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"one-byte-data\"></a>\n\n## One-Byte data\n\n```\nRequest: [AORAND;AL1;]\n\nResponse: [AORAND;AK61;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"10-byte-data\"></a>\n\n## 10-Byte data\n\n```\nRequest: [AORAND;AL10;]\n\nResponse: [AORAND;AKB00149DEF90ACE31C3DC;]\n```\n"
