    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# RASY: Get PKI Key Cryptogram from the Key Table\n\nFuente: [RASY: Get PKI Key Cryptogram from the Key Table](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/key_tables/rasy-get-pki-key-cryptogram-from-the-key-table)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:08:28.100Z\n\n---\n\nThis command takes in a PKI key slot and returns the key encrypted under the specified major key.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This command supports Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC) keys. You must enable the PQC license to use these keys.\n- Recovering PQC keys from board slots is currently disabled in PCI HSM mode pending PCI approval.\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| ECC | Enables commands requiring Elliptic Curve Cryptography (ECC) functionality. |\n| RSA | Enables commands requiring RSA functionality. |\n\n<a id=\"optional-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Optional licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| PQC | Enables Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC) commands and functionality. |\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Keys | View key and table information | Mgmt | 0 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `RD` | PKI key slot | Numeric | 1-4 | Yes |\n| `FS` | Major Key that token RD is encrypted under | Numeric | 1 | Optional |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `RD` | Encrypted PKI key | Hexadecimal | Variable |\n| `BB` | Key type | Alphanumeric | <br><br>1<br><br>17<br><br> |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RASY` |\n\n<a id=\"rd-pki-key-slot\"></a>\n\n### RD - PKI key slot\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-major-key-that-token-rd-is-encrypted-under\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - Major Key that token RD is encrypted under\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: MFK (default)<br>`6`: PMK<br>`7`: FTK (if PKCS #11 is available) |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RASY` |\n\n<a id=\"rd-encrypted-pki-key\"></a>\n\n### RD - Encrypted PKI key\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Variable | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"bb-key-type\"></a>\n\n### BB - Key type\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1<br>17 | Alphanumeric | `1`: Private key<br>`2`: Public key<br>`INDEX KEY MISSING`: Key not found in the specified key slot |\n\n<a id=\"command-example\"></a>\n\n## Command example\n\n<a id=\"example-1\"></a>\n\n### Example 1\n\n```\nRequest: [AORASY;RD0;FS6;]\n\nResponse: [AORASY;;BB1;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"pcq\"></a>\n\n### PCQ\n\n```\nRequest: [AORASY;RD1;FS6;]\n\nResponse: [AORASY;;BB1;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"test-key-used\"></a>\n\n### Test Key Used\n\nPMK Test Key: 8888888888888888 AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF 1111111111111111 Check Digit: (financial 1E26) (cmac 3B5E)\n\n<a id=\"changelog\"></a>\n\n## Changelog\n\n2024-07-03\n\n- Added **FW-14467** | Added support for recovering PQC keys from board slots. (Disabled in PCI HSM Mode Pending PCI Approval)\n",
      "en": "# RASY: Get PKI Key Cryptogram from the Key Table\n\nFuente: [RASY: Get PKI Key Cryptogram from the Key Table](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/key_tables/rasy-get-pki-key-cryptogram-from-the-key-table)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:08:28.100Z\n\n---\n\nThis command takes in a PKI key slot and returns the key encrypted under the specified major key.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This command supports Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC) keys. You must enable the PQC license to use these keys.\n- Recovering PQC keys from board slots is currently disabled in PCI HSM mode pending PCI approval.\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| ECC | Enables commands requiring Elliptic Curve Cryptography (ECC) functionality. |\n| RSA | Enables commands requiring RSA functionality. |\n\n<a id=\"optional-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Optional licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| PQC | Enables Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC) commands and functionality. |\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Keys | View key and table information | Mgmt | 0 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `RD` | PKI key slot | Numeric | 1-4 | Yes |\n| `FS` | Major Key that token RD is encrypted under | Numeric | 1 | Optional |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `RD` | Encrypted PKI key | Hexadecimal | Variable |\n| `BB` | Key type | Alphanumeric | <br><br>1<br><br>17<br><br> |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RASY` |\n\n<a id=\"rd-pki-key-slot\"></a>\n\n### RD - PKI key slot\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-major-key-that-token-rd-is-encrypted-under\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - Major Key that token RD is encrypted under\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: MFK (default)<br>`6`: PMK<br>`7`: FTK (if PKCS #11 is available) |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RASY` |\n\n<a id=\"rd-encrypted-pki-key\"></a>\n\n### RD - Encrypted PKI key\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Variable | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"bb-key-type\"></a>\n\n### BB - Key type\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1<br>17 | Alphanumeric | `1`: Private key<br>`2`: Public key<br>`INDEX KEY MISSING`: Key not found in the specified key slot |\n\n<a id=\"command-example\"></a>\n\n## Command example\n\n<a id=\"example-1\"></a>\n\n### Example 1\n\n```\nRequest: [AORASY;RD0;FS6;]\n\nResponse: [AORASY;;BB1;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"pcq\"></a>\n\n### PCQ\n\n```\nRequest: [AORASY;RD1;FS6;]\n\nResponse: [AORASY;;BB1;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"test-key-used\"></a>\n\n### Test Key Used\n\nPMK Test Key: 8888888888888888 AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF 1111111111111111 Check Digit: (financial 1E26) (cmac 3B5E)\n\n<a id=\"changelog\"></a>\n\n## Changelog\n\n2024-07-03\n\n- Added **FW-14467** | Added support for recovering PQC keys from board slots. (Disabled in PCI HSM Mode Pending PCI Approval)\n"
    }
