    "source": "Futurex Excrypt Command Reference Manual v7.6.1 (RDPK)",
    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# RDPK: Decrypt Public Key and Output in DER Format\n\nFuente: [RDPK: Decrypt Public Key and Output in DER Format](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/key_tables/rdpk-decrypt-public-key-and-output-in-der-format)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:08:31.190Z\n\n---\n\nThis command decrypts a public key under the MFK and outputs it in the clear in DER format.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- **Key slot offsets** differ between the API and Excrypt. While the API recognizes PKI storage to be key slots 0-99, the Excrypt Manager loads keys into slots 1-100. Therefore, for tokens that support PKI storage table indexing, the key slot in which the key is loaded using Excrypt Manager is off by one (for example, a key loaded into slot **1** on the Excrypt Manager is referenced on the API as slot **0**).\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| RSA | Enables commands requiring RSA functionality. |\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Keys | View key and table information | Mgmt | 0 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `FS` | Major key that token SD is encrypted under | Numeric | 1 | Optional |\n| `SD` | Public key encrypted under modifier 1 of the major key | Hexadecimal | 1-4096 | Yes |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `RD` | Clear public key | Hexadecimal | 2-4096 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RDPK` |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-major-key-that-token-sd-is-encrypted-under\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - Major key that token SD is encrypted under\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: MFK (default)<br>`6`: PMK<br>`7`: FTK (If PKCS #11 is available) |\n\n<a id=\"sd-public-key-encrypted-under-modifier-1-of-the-major-key\"></a>\n\n### SD - Public key encrypted under modifier 1 of the major key\n\nKey slot 0-99 might be referenced (see the preceding note about **key slot offsets**).\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4096 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id-2\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RDPK` |\n\n<a id=\"rd-clear-public-key\"></a>\n\n### RD - Clear public key\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2-4096 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"command-example\"></a>\n\n## Command example\n\n```\nRequest: [AORDPK;SD701CE18FEC0C00B234495BC9A6EB5FE429FD2A3991208B30AA3BE25558E2C9A8A787B1E55082A49111ED70B5C61E945B0E5C38DFEFBB83594072276E54F21477E8CC5CB6107B175A15ECB6F8FD53F3EF;]\n\nResponse: [AORDPK;RD3048024100C6ED70390B73CDA5F197A86E7AFF5A39A3A01B8C0B72B9A184B3B0522512591F6E83DF624ED95A097A0CFB4F355B088BA300BD9F413F406C7D7C00AA8C2140390203010001;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"test-key-used\"></a>\n\n### Test Key Used\n\nMFK Test Key: D2DE5CD9110F4CAB 1111111111111111 0123456789ABCDEF Check Digit: (financial 8071) (cmac 9652)\n",
      "en": "# RDPK: Decrypt Public Key and Output in DER Format\n\nFuente: [RDPK: Decrypt Public Key and Output in DER Format](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/key_tables/rdpk-decrypt-public-key-and-output-in-der-format)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:08:31.190Z\n\n---\n\nThis command decrypts a public key under the MFK and outputs it in the clear in DER format.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- **Key slot offsets** differ between the API and Excrypt. While the API recognizes PKI storage to be key slots 0-99, the Excrypt Manager loads keys into slots 1-100. Therefore, for tokens that support PKI storage table indexing, the key slot in which the key is loaded using Excrypt Manager is off by one (for example, a key loaded into slot **1** on the Excrypt Manager is referenced on the API as slot **0**).\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| RSA | Enables commands requiring RSA functionality. |\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Keys | View key and table information | Mgmt | 0 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `FS` | Major key that token SD is encrypted under | Numeric | 1 | Optional |\n| `SD` | Public key encrypted under modifier 1 of the major key | Hexadecimal | 1-4096 | Yes |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `RD` | Clear public key | Hexadecimal | 2-4096 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RDPK` |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-major-key-that-token-sd-is-encrypted-under\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - Major key that token SD is encrypted under\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: MFK (default)<br>`6`: PMK<br>`7`: FTK (If PKCS #11 is available) |\n\n<a id=\"sd-public-key-encrypted-under-modifier-1-of-the-major-key\"></a>\n\n### SD - Public key encrypted under modifier 1 of the major key\n\nKey slot 0-99 might be referenced (see the preceding note about **key slot offsets**).\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4096 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id-2\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RDPK` |\n\n<a id=\"rd-clear-public-key\"></a>\n\n### RD - Clear public key\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2-4096 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"command-example\"></a>\n\n## Command example\n\n```\nRequest: [AORDPK;SD701CE18FEC0C00B234495BC9A6EB5FE429FD2A3991208B30AA3BE25558E2C9A8A787B1E55082A49111ED70B5C61E945B0E5C38DFEFBB83594072276E54F21477E8CC5CB6107B175A15ECB6F8FD53F3EF;]\n\nResponse: [AORDPK;RD3048024100C6ED70390B73CDA5F197A86E7AFF5A39A3A01B8C0B72B9A184B3B0522512591F6E83DF624ED95A097A0CFB4F355B088BA300BD9F413F406C7D7C00AA8C2140390203010001;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"test-key-used\"></a>\n\n### Test Key Used\n\nMFK Test Key: D2DE5CD9110F4CAB 1111111111111111 0123456789ABCDEF Check Digit: (financial 8071) (cmac 9652)\n"
    }
