      "es": "# REPK: Encrypt Public Key\n\nFuente: [REPK: Encrypt Public Key](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/key_tables/repk-encrypt-public-key)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:08:31.123Z\n\n---\n\nThis command encrypts a clear public key in DER formatting into a trusted public key under the specified major key. It requires a trusted connection and the RSA ability.\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| RSA | Enables commands requiring RSA functionality. |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `FS` | Major key that RD is under | Numeric | 1 | Optional |\n| `RD` | Clear public key in DER formatting | Hexadecimal | Variable | Yes |\n| `CZ` | Usage for generated key | Alphabetic | 1 | If non-MFK |\n| `SF` | Security usage for generated key | Numeric | 1 | If non-MFK |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `SD` | Trusted public key | Hexadecimal | Variable |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| **Length** | **Data Type** | **Accepted Values** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `REPK` |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-major-key-that-rd-is-under\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - Major key that RD is under\n\n| **Length** | **Data Type** | **Accepted Values** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: MFK (default)<br>`6`: PMK<br>`7`: FTK (if PKCS11 is available) |\n\n<a id=\"rd-clear-public-key-in-der-formatting\"></a>\n\n### RD - Clear public key in DER formatting\n\n| **Length** | **Data Type** | **Accepted Values** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Variable | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"optional-non-mfk-cz-usage-for-generated-key\"></a>\n\n### (Optional, Non-MFK) CZ - Usage for generated key\n\nREPK loads a public key, so only public-key-compatible usages are accepted. See [Key usage constants](../../concepts/Key_usage_constants.md) for the full table.\n\n| **Length** | **Data Type** | **Accepted Values** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Alphabetic | `E`: Encrypt<br>`V`: Verify<br>`X`: Derive<br>`1`: Asymmetric Wrap |\n\n<a id=\"optional-non-mfk-sf-security-usage-for-generated-key\"></a>\n\n### (Optional, Non-MFK) SF - Security usage for generated key\n\nCombine flags by summing their values. See [Security usage flags](../../concepts/Security_usage_flags.md) for full descriptions.\n\n| **Length** | **Data Type** | **Accepted Values** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `0`: None<br>`1`: Private<br>`2`: Sensitive<br>`4`: Immutable |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| **Length** | **Data Type** | Returned Value |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `REPK` |\n\n<a id=\"sd-trusted-public-key\"></a>\n\n### SD - Trusted public key\n\nEncrypted under the MFK in the requested key block method.\n\n| **Length** | **Data Type** | Returned Value |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Variable | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n",
      "en": "# REPK: Encrypt Public Key\n\nFuente: [REPK: Encrypt Public Key](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/key_tables/repk-encrypt-public-key)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:08:31.123Z\n\n---\n\nThis command encrypts a clear public key in DER formatting into a trusted public key under the specified major key. It requires a trusted connection and the RSA ability.\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| RSA | Enables commands requiring RSA functionality. |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `FS` | Major key that RD is under | Numeric | 1 | Optional |\n| `RD` | Clear public key in DER formatting | Hexadecimal | Variable | Yes |\n| `CZ` | Usage for generated key | Alphabetic | 1 | If non-MFK |\n| `SF` | Security usage for generated key | Numeric | 1 | If non-MFK |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `SD` | Trusted public key | Hexadecimal | Variable |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| **Length** | **Data Type** | **Accepted Values** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `REPK` |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-major-key-that-rd-is-under\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - Major key that RD is under\n\n| **Length** | **Data Type** | **Accepted Values** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: MFK (default)<br>`6`: PMK<br>`7`: FTK (if PKCS11 is available) |\n\n<a id=\"rd-clear-public-key-in-der-formatting\"></a>\n\n### RD - Clear public key in DER formatting\n\n| **Length** | **Data Type** | **Accepted Values** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Variable | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"optional-non-mfk-cz-usage-for-generated-key\"></a>\n\n### (Optional, Non-MFK) CZ - Usage for generated key\n\nREPK loads a public key, so only public-key-compatible usages are accepted. See [Key usage constants](../../concepts/Key_usage_constants.md) for the full table.\n\n| **Length** | **Data Type** | **Accepted Values** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Alphabetic | `E`: Encrypt<br>`V`: Verify<br>`X`: Derive<br>`1`: Asymmetric Wrap |\n\n<a id=\"optional-non-mfk-sf-security-usage-for-generated-key\"></a>\n\n### (Optional, Non-MFK) SF - Security usage for generated key\n\nCombine flags by summing their values. See [Security usage flags](../../concepts/Security_usage_flags.md) for full descriptions.\n\n| **Length** | **Data Type** | **Accepted Values** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `0`: None<br>`1`: Private<br>`2`: Sensitive<br>`4`: Immutable |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| **Length** | **Data Type** | Returned Value |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `REPK` |\n\n<a id=\"sd-trusted-public-key\"></a>\n\n### SD - Trusted public key\n\nEncrypted under the MFK in the requested key block method.\n\n| **Length** | **Data Type** | Returned Value |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Variable | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n"
