    "summary": {
      "es": "This command restores a key table using a backup key.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This command is used in conjunction with the command **BACK**, which facilitates backups of the key storage table.\n- Command **BACK** responds with encrypted data under a backup key sent in the **CI** and **CJ** tokens. The data returned in the **CI** and **CJ** tokens should be referenced when performing this command.\n- To restore the information backed up using command **BACK** to another HSM using this command, the recipient HSM must contain the same backup key as the original HSM. If it does not, the recipient HSM will respond with an error message.",
      "en": "This command restores a key table using a backup key.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This command is used in conjunction with the command **BACK**, which facilitates backups of the key storage table.\n- Command **BACK** responds with encrypted data under a backup key sent in the **CI** and **CJ** tokens. The data returned in the **CI** and **CJ** tokens should be referenced when performing this command.\n- To restore the information backed up using command **BACK** to another HSM using this command, the recipient HSM must contain the same backup key as the original HSM. If it does not, the recipient HSM will respond with an error message."
    },
