    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# REST: Restore Key Table\n\nFuente: [REST: Restore Key Table](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/lifecycle/rest-restore-key-table)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:08:32.584Z\n\n---\n\nThis command restores a key table using a backup key.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This command is used in conjunction with the command **BACK**, which facilitates backups of the key storage table.\n- Command **BACK** responds with encrypted data under a backup key sent in the **CI** and **CJ** tokens. The data returned in the **CI** and **CJ** tokens should be referenced when performing this command.\n- To restore the information backed up using command **BACK** to another HSM using this command, the recipient HSM must contain the same backup key as the original HSM. If it does not, the recipient HSM will respond with an error message.\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Backup:Restore Keys | Restore a keys backup that was previously taken. | Mgmt | 2 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `CI` | Location and modifier information | Hexadecimal | 16 | Yes |\n| `CJ` | Key Block Information on a key slot | Hexadecimal | 7-6000 | Yes |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `BB` | Ending indicator | Alphabetic | 2 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `REST` |\n\n<a id=\"ci-location-and-modifier-information\"></a>\n\n### CI - Location and modifier information\n\nReferenced from command **BACK** in request token **CI**.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"cj-key-block-information-on-a-key-slot\"></a>\n\n### CJ - Key Block Information on a key slot\n\nReferenced from Excrypt command **BACK**in request token **CJ**.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 7-6000 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"response-token\"></a>\n\n## Response token\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `REST` |\n\n<a id=\"bb-ending-indicator\"></a>\n\n### BB - Ending indicator\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2 | Alphabetic | `OK`: Key slot restoration successful |\n\n<a id=\"command-example\"></a>\n\n## Command example\n\n```\nRequest: [AOREST;CI761023A5C4D10DD3;CJ1KDEE000,EE3683F3E84A5765B49DE4615FB430BAF5A08325A93722C0,686520BFEA3E08D9;]\n\nResponse: [AOREST;BBOK;]\n```\n",
      "en": "# REST: Restore Key Table\n\nFuente: [REST: Restore Key Table](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/lifecycle/rest-restore-key-table)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:08:32.584Z\n\n---\n\nThis command restores a key table using a backup key.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- This command is used in conjunction with the command **BACK**, which facilitates backups of the key storage table.\n- Command **BACK** responds with encrypted data under a backup key sent in the **CI** and **CJ** tokens. The data returned in the **CI** and **CJ** tokens should be referenced when performing this command.\n- To restore the information backed up using command **BACK** to another HSM using this command, the recipient HSM must contain the same backup key as the original HSM. If it does not, the recipient HSM will respond with an error message.\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Backup:Restore Keys | Restore a keys backup that was previously taken. | Mgmt | 2 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `CI` | Location and modifier information | Hexadecimal | 16 | Yes |\n| `CJ` | Key Block Information on a key slot | Hexadecimal | 7-6000 | Yes |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `BB` | Ending indicator | Alphabetic | 2 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `REST` |\n\n<a id=\"ci-location-and-modifier-information\"></a>\n\n### CI - Location and modifier information\n\nReferenced from command **BACK** in request token **CI**.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"cj-key-block-information-on-a-key-slot\"></a>\n\n### CJ - Key Block Information on a key slot\n\nReferenced from Excrypt command **BACK**in request token **CJ**.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 7-6000 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"response-token\"></a>\n\n## Response token\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `REST` |\n\n<a id=\"bb-ending-indicator\"></a>\n\n### BB - Ending indicator\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2 | Alphabetic | `OK`: Key slot restoration successful |\n\n<a id=\"command-example\"></a>\n\n## Command example\n\n```\nRequest: [AOREST;CI761023A5C4D10DD3;CJ1KDEE000,EE3683F3E84A5765B49DE4615FB430BAF5A08325A93722C0,686520BFEA3E08D9;]\n\nResponse: [AOREST;BBOK;]\n```\n"
    }
