    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# RKBD: Get HSM Serial Number\n\nFuente: [RKBD: Get HSM Serial Number](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/system/utility/rkbd-get-hsm-serial-number)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:08:34.081Z\n\n---\n\nThis command simply echoes back what was sent. This command enables you to send commands directly to an HSM instead of a Guardian without needing to modify what commands are sent.\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `FS` | No Functionality | Alphanumeric | 1-16 | Optional |\n| `GA` | No Functionality | Alphanumeric | 1-16 | Optional |\n| `OS` | No Functionality | Alphanumeric | 1-16 | Optional |\n| `BK` | No Functionality | Alphanumeric | 1-16 | Optional |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `AN` | Response Code | Alphabetic | 1 |\n| `FS` | Returns what was sent | Alphanumeric | 1-16 |\n| `GA` | Returns what was sent | Alphanumeric | 1-16 |\n| `OS` | Returns what was sent | Alphanumeric | 1-16 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RKBD` |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-no-functionality\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - No Functionality\n\nReturned in response with same value if sent.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-16 | Alphanumeric | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"optional-ga-no-functionality\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) GA - No Functionality\n\nReturned in response with same value if sent.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-16 | Alphanumeric | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"optional-os-no-functionality\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) OS - No Functionality\n\nReturned in response with same value if sent.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-16 | Alphanumeric | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"optional-bk-no-functionality\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) BK - No Functionality\n\nThis is not returned in the response.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-16 | Alphanumeric | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RKBD` |\n\n<a id=\"an-response-code\"></a>\n\n### AN - Response Code\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Alphabetic | `Y`: Succeeded<br>`N`: Failed |\n\n<a id=\"fs-returns-what-was-sent\"></a>\n\n### FS - Returns what was sent\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-16 | Alphanumeric | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"ga-returns-what-was-sent\"></a>\n\n### GA - Returns what was sent\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-16 | Alphanumeric | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"os-returns-what-was-sent\"></a>\n\n### OS - Returns what was sent\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-16 | Alphanumeric | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"example-1\"></a>\n\n### Example 1\n\n```\nRequest: [AORKBD;]\n\nResponse: [AORKBD;ANY;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"example-2\"></a>\n\n### Example 2\n\n```\nRequest: [AORKBD;FSAABB;]\n\nResponse: [AORKBD;ANY;FSAABB;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"example-3\"></a>\n\n### Example 3\n\n```\nRequest: [AORKBD;FS12;GA88;]\n\nResponse: [AORKBD;ANY;FS12;GA88;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"example-4\"></a>\n\n### Example 4\n\n```\nRequest: [AORKBD;FS2;GA1829832362;OS1;BK1;]\n\nResponse: [AORKBD;ANY;FS2;GA1829832362;OS1;]\n```\n",
      "en": "# RKBD: Get HSM Serial Number\n\nFuente: [RKBD: Get HSM Serial Number](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/system/utility/rkbd-get-hsm-serial-number)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:08:34.081Z\n\n---\n\nThis command simply echoes back what was sent. This command enables you to send commands directly to an HSM instead of a Guardian without needing to modify what commands are sent.\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `FS` | No Functionality | Alphanumeric | 1-16 | Optional |\n| `GA` | No Functionality | Alphanumeric | 1-16 | Optional |\n| `OS` | No Functionality | Alphanumeric | 1-16 | Optional |\n| `BK` | No Functionality | Alphanumeric | 1-16 | Optional |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `AN` | Response Code | Alphabetic | 1 |\n| `FS` | Returns what was sent | Alphanumeric | 1-16 |\n| `GA` | Returns what was sent | Alphanumeric | 1-16 |\n| `OS` | Returns what was sent | Alphanumeric | 1-16 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RKBD` |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-no-functionality\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - No Functionality\n\nReturned in response with same value if sent.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-16 | Alphanumeric | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"optional-ga-no-functionality\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) GA - No Functionality\n\nReturned in response with same value if sent.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-16 | Alphanumeric | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"optional-os-no-functionality\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) OS - No Functionality\n\nReturned in response with same value if sent.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-16 | Alphanumeric | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"optional-bk-no-functionality\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) BK - No Functionality\n\nThis is not returned in the response.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-16 | Alphanumeric | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RKBD` |\n\n<a id=\"an-response-code\"></a>\n\n### AN - Response Code\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Alphabetic | `Y`: Succeeded<br>`N`: Failed |\n\n<a id=\"fs-returns-what-was-sent\"></a>\n\n### FS - Returns what was sent\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-16 | Alphanumeric | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"ga-returns-what-was-sent\"></a>\n\n### GA - Returns what was sent\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-16 | Alphanumeric | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"os-returns-what-was-sent\"></a>\n\n### OS - Returns what was sent\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-16 | Alphanumeric | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"example-1\"></a>\n\n### Example 1\n\n```\nRequest: [AORKBD;]\n\nResponse: [AORKBD;ANY;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"example-2\"></a>\n\n### Example 2\n\n```\nRequest: [AORKBD;FSAABB;]\n\nResponse: [AORKBD;ANY;FSAABB;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"example-3\"></a>\n\n### Example 3\n\n```\nRequest: [AORKBD;FS12;GA88;]\n\nResponse: [AORKBD;ANY;FS12;GA88;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"example-4\"></a>\n\n### Example 4\n\n```\nRequest: [AORKBD;FS2;GA1829832362;OS1;BK1;]\n\nResponse: [AORKBD;ANY;FS2;GA1829832362;OS1;]\n```\n"
    }
