    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# RPFP: Get Public Key from Private Key Index\n\nFuente: [RPFP: Get Public Key from Private Key Index](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/key_tables/rpfp-get-public-key-from-private-key-index)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:08:37.098Z\n\n---\n\nThis command gets a public key from a private key encrypted under the MFK or a private key index.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The **Key slot offset** differs between the API and Excrypt. While the API recognizes PKI storage to be slots 0-99, the Excrypt Manager loads keys into slots 1-100. Therefore, for tokens that support PKI storage table indexing, the key slot in which the key is loaded using Excrypt Manager is off by one (for example, a key loaded into slot **1** on the Excrypt Manager is referenced in the API as slot **0**).\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| RSA | Enables commands requiring RSA functionality. |\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Keys | View key and table information | Mgmt | 0 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RPFP` |\n\n<a id=\"rc-private-key-encrypted-under-the-major-key\"></a>\n\n### RC - Private Key encrypted under the major key\n\nYou can reference key slot 0-99 (see the preceding note about **key slot offsets**).\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-6144 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"ak-output-type\"></a>\n\n### AK - Output Type\n\n**Note** Trusted Public Key output must be under dual control if the legacy RSA configuration option is disabled.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: Output Clear Public Key in DER format<br>`2`: Output Trusted Public Key |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-major-key-that-rc-is-encrypted-under\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - Major Key that RC is encrypted under\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: MFK (default)<br>`6`: PMK<br>`7`: FTK (If PKCS #11 is available) |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RPFP` |\n\n<a id=\"ak-output-type-2\"></a>\n\n### AK - Output type\n\n**Note** The Output of the encrypted public key is only available when the RSA legacy mode is enabled.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: Clear Public Key in DER format<br>`2`: Trusted Public Key<br>`3`: Internal error |\n\n<a id=\"rd-public-key\"></a>\n\n### RD - Public Key\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-6144 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"output-clear-public-key\"></a>\n\n### Output Clear Public Key\n\n```\nRequest: [AORPFP;RC4;AK1;]\n\nResponse: [AORPFP;AK1;;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"output-trusted-public-key\"></a>\n\n### Output Trusted Public Key\n\n```\nRequest: [AORPFP;RC4;AK2;]\n\nResponse: [AORPFP;AK2;;]\n```\n",
      "en": "# RPFP: Get Public Key from Private Key Index\n\nFuente: [RPFP: Get Public Key from Private Key Index](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/key_tables/rpfp-get-public-key-from-private-key-index)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:08:37.098Z\n\n---\n\nThis command gets a public key from a private key encrypted under the MFK or a private key index.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The **Key slot offset** differs between the API and Excrypt. While the API recognizes PKI storage to be slots 0-99, the Excrypt Manager loads keys into slots 1-100. Therefore, for tokens that support PKI storage table indexing, the key slot in which the key is loaded using Excrypt Manager is off by one (for example, a key loaded into slot **1** on the Excrypt Manager is referenced in the API as slot **0**).\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| RSA | Enables commands requiring RSA functionality. |\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Keys | View key and table information | Mgmt | 0 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RPFP` |\n\n<a id=\"rc-private-key-encrypted-under-the-major-key\"></a>\n\n### RC - Private Key encrypted under the major key\n\nYou can reference key slot 0-99 (see the preceding note about **key slot offsets**).\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-6144 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"ak-output-type\"></a>\n\n### AK - Output Type\n\n**Note** Trusted Public Key output must be under dual control if the legacy RSA configuration option is disabled.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: Output Clear Public Key in DER format<br>`2`: Output Trusted Public Key |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-major-key-that-rc-is-encrypted-under\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - Major Key that RC is encrypted under\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: MFK (default)<br>`6`: PMK<br>`7`: FTK (If PKCS #11 is available) |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RPFP` |\n\n<a id=\"ak-output-type-2\"></a>\n\n### AK - Output type\n\n**Note** The Output of the encrypted public key is only available when the RSA legacy mode is enabled.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: Clear Public Key in DER format<br>`2`: Trusted Public Key<br>`3`: Internal error |\n\n<a id=\"rd-public-key\"></a>\n\n### RD - Public Key\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-6144 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"output-clear-public-key\"></a>\n\n### Output Clear Public Key\n\n```\nRequest: [AORPFP;RC4;AK1;]\n\nResponse: [AORPFP;AK1;;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"output-trusted-public-key\"></a>\n\n### Output Trusted Public Key\n\n```\nRequest: [AORPFP;RC4;AK2;]\n\nResponse: [AORPFP;AK2;;]\n```\n"
    }
