    "source": "Futurex Excrypt Command Reference Manual v7.6.1 (RRSA)",
    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# RRSA: Retrieve PKI Key Cryptogram from Key Table\n\nFuente: [RRSA: Retrieve PKI Key Cryptogram from Key Table](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/key_tables/rrsa-retrieve-pki-key-cryptogram-from-key-table)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:08:41.220Z\n\n---\n\nThis command retrieves a PKI key cryptogram from the key table.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The **Key slot offset** differs between the API and Excrypt. While the API recognizes PKI storage to be slots 0-99, the Excrypt Manager loads keys into slots 1-100. Therefore, for tokens that support PKI storage table indexing, the key slot in which the key is loaded using Excrypt Manager is off by one (for example, a key loaded into slot **1** on the Excrypt Manager is referenced in the API as slot **0**).\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| RSA | Enables commands requiring RSA functionality. |\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Keys | View key and table information | Mgmt | 0 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `RD` | Key slot of the key being referenced | Numeric | 1-2 | Yes |\n| `FS` | Major key that token RD is under | Numeric | 1 | Optional |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `RD` | Public or private key in the specified key slot | Hexadecimal | <br><br>0<br><br>Variable<br><br> |\n| `BB` | Key type | Numeric | <br><br>0<br><br>1<br><br> |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RRSA` |\n\n<a id=\"rd-key-slot-of-the-key-being-referenced\"></a>\n\n### RD - Key slot of the key being referenced\n\nSee the preceding note about **key slot offsets**.\n\n**Note** If the key slot is empty, response tokens **RD** and **BB** are empty.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-2 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-major-key-that-token-rd-is-under\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - Major key that token RD is under\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: MFK (default)<br>`6`: PMK<br>`7`: FTK (If PKCS #11 is available) |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RRSA` |\n\n<a id=\"rd-public-or-private-key-in-the-specified-key-slot\"></a>\n\n### RD - Public or Private Key in the specified key slot\n\nIf it is a Public Key, then the cryptogram is encrypted under modifier 1 of the major key.\n\nIf it is a Private Key, it is under the clear major key.\n\n**Note** This field is empty if the key slot is empty.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 0<br>Variable | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"bb-key-type\"></a>\n\n### BB - Key Type\n\n**Note** This field is empty if the key slot is empty.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 0<br>1 | Numeric | `1`: Private Key<br>`2`: Public Key |\n\n<a id=\"command-example\"></a>\n\n## Command example\n\n```\nRequest: [AORRSA;RD4;]\n\nResponse: [AORRSA;;BB1;]\n```\n",
      "en": "# RRSA: Retrieve PKI Key Cryptogram from Key Table\n\nFuente: [RRSA: Retrieve PKI Key Cryptogram from Key Table](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/key_tables/rrsa-retrieve-pki-key-cryptogram-from-key-table)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:08:41.220Z\n\n---\n\nThis command retrieves a PKI key cryptogram from the key table.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The **Key slot offset** differs between the API and Excrypt. While the API recognizes PKI storage to be slots 0-99, the Excrypt Manager loads keys into slots 1-100. Therefore, for tokens that support PKI storage table indexing, the key slot in which the key is loaded using Excrypt Manager is off by one (for example, a key loaded into slot **1** on the Excrypt Manager is referenced in the API as slot **0**).\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| RSA | Enables commands requiring RSA functionality. |\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Keys | View key and table information | Mgmt | 0 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `RD` | Key slot of the key being referenced | Numeric | 1-2 | Yes |\n| `FS` | Major key that token RD is under | Numeric | 1 | Optional |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `RD` | Public or private key in the specified key slot | Hexadecimal | <br><br>0<br><br>Variable<br><br> |\n| `BB` | Key type | Numeric | <br><br>0<br><br>1<br><br> |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RRSA` |\n\n<a id=\"rd-key-slot-of-the-key-being-referenced\"></a>\n\n### RD - Key slot of the key being referenced\n\nSee the preceding note about **key slot offsets**.\n\n**Note** If the key slot is empty, response tokens **RD** and **BB** are empty.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-2 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-major-key-that-token-rd-is-under\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - Major key that token RD is under\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: MFK (default)<br>`6`: PMK<br>`7`: FTK (If PKCS #11 is available) |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `RRSA` |\n\n<a id=\"rd-public-or-private-key-in-the-specified-key-slot\"></a>\n\n### RD - Public or Private Key in the specified key slot\n\nIf it is a Public Key, then the cryptogram is encrypted under modifier 1 of the major key.\n\nIf it is a Private Key, it is under the clear major key.\n\n**Note** This field is empty if the key slot is empty.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 0<br>Variable | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"bb-key-type\"></a>\n\n### BB - Key Type\n\n**Note** This field is empty if the key slot is empty.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 0<br>1 | Numeric | `1`: Private Key<br>`2`: Public Key |\n\n<a id=\"command-example\"></a>\n\n## Command example\n\n```\nRequest: [AORRSA;RD4;]\n\nResponse: [AORRSA;;BB1;]\n```\n"
    }
