    "name": {
      "es": "RUPT: NPCI UPI data translation",
      "en": "RUPT: NPCI UPI data translation"
    },
    "summary": {
      "es": "This command handles a Unified Payments Interface (UPI) mobile PIN (MPIN) that arrives encrypted under an RSA key. By default it decrypts the MPIN block with the private key in `RC` and re-encrypts it under the trusted public key in `RD`, returning the new block in `MP`. When token `BJ` is `1` and the CPIN license is enabled, it instead returns the clear MPIN in `MP`. Both modes also echo the parameter block in `PB` and return the decrypted encrypted block in `EB`.\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in PCI HSM Mode",
      "en": "This command handles a Unified Payments Interface (UPI) mobile PIN (MPIN) that arrives encrypted under an RSA key. By default it decrypts the MPIN block with the private key in `RC` and re-encrypts it under the trusted public key in `RD`, returning the new block in `MP`. When token `BJ` is `1` and the CPIN license is enabled, it instead returns the clear MPIN in `MP`. Both modes also echo the parameter block in `PB` and return the decrypted encrypted block in `EB`.\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in PCI HSM Mode"
    },
    "description": {
      "es": "This command handles a Unified Payments Interface (UPI) mobile PIN (MPIN) that arrives encrypted under an RSA key. By default it decrypts the MPIN block with the private key in `RC` and re-encrypts it under the trusted public key in `RD`, returning the new block in `MP`. When token `BJ` is `1` and the CPIN license is enabled, it instead returns the clear MPIN in `MP`. Both modes also echo the parameter block in `PB` and return the decrypted encrypted block in `EB`.\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in PCI HSM Mode",
      "en": "This command handles a Unified Payments Interface (UPI) mobile PIN (MPIN) that arrives encrypted under an RSA key. By default it decrypts the MPIN block with the private key in `RC` and re-encrypts it under the trusted public key in `RD`, returning the new block in `MP`. When token `BJ` is `1` and the CPIN license is enabled, it instead returns the clear MPIN in `MP`. Both modes also echo the parameter block in `PB` and return the decrypted encrypted block in `EB`.\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in PCI HSM Mode"
    },
