      "en": "This command verifies a PKCS #7 or X.509 certificate and returns the public key encrypted under the specified major key.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- If ***RSA Legacy Functionality*** is enabled, the trusted public key (token **SA**) is optional.\n- The **Key slot offset** differs between the API and Excrypt. While the API recognizes PKI storage to be slots 0-99, the Excrypt Manager loads keys into slots 1-100. Therefore, for tokens that support PKI storage table indexing, the key slot in which the key is loaded using Excrypt Manager is off by one (for example, a key loaded into slot **1** on the Excrypt Manager is referenced in the API as slot **0**).\n- You can enable ***AVPC/RVPC Ignore Certificate Expiration*** under Function Settings on the Web Portal to ignore the validity date check."
