      "es": "# SMFK: Switch Major Key with KEK\n\nFuente: [SMFK: Switch Major Key with KEK](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/translate/smfk-switch-major-key-with-kek)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:09:19.367Z\n\n---\n\nThis command switches a major key to the KEK slot and converts the key table stored on the HSM to encryption under the new major key.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permissions | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Major Keys:Rotate | Switch the MFK and the Pending-MFK. | Mgmt | 2 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `SMFK` |\n\n<a id=\"optional-bj-operation\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) BJ - Operation\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `0`: Switch Major Key and KEK (default)<br>`1`: Return the key table status only |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-major-key-to-be-rotated-with-kek\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - Major Key to be rotated with KEK\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: MFK (default)<br>`6`: PMK<br>`7`: FTK (if PKCS11 is available) |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `SMFK` |\n\n<a id=\"bb-success-indicator\"></a>\n\n### BB - Success Indicator\n\nReturned only when request token **BJ** is `0`.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Alphabetic | `Y`: Conversion was successful<br>`N`: Conversion was not successful |\n\n<a id=\"fs-key-table-status\"></a>\n\n### FS - Key Table Status\n\nReturned only when request token **BJ** is `1`.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `0`: Key table not locked<br>`1`: Key table locked |\n\n<a id=\"sw-list-all-swappable-slots-with-kek\"></a>\n\n### SW - List all swappable slots with KEK\n\nReturned only when request token **BJ** is `-1`.\n\nReturned empty if nothing can be swapped.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Variable | ASCII | A - Z, a - z, 0 - 9 except ; [ ] |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"switch-the-mfk/kek-and-translate-the-keys\"></a>\n\n### Switch the MFK/KEK and translate the keys\n\n```\nRequest: [AOSMFK;]\n\nResponse: [AOSMFK;BBY;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"status-request-of-the-key-table-not-locked\"></a>\n\n### Status request of the key table (not locked)\n\n```\nRequest: [AOSMFK;BJ1;]\n\nResponse: [AOSMFK;FS0;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"status-request-of-the-key-table-locked\"></a>\n\n### Status request of the key table (locked)\n\n```\nRequest: [AOSMFK;BJ1;]\n\nResponse: [AOSMFK;FS1;]\n```\n",
      "en": "# SMFK: Switch Major Key with KEK\n\nFuente: [SMFK: Switch Major Key with KEK](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/translate/smfk-switch-major-key-with-kek)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:09:19.367Z\n\n---\n\nThis command switches a major key to the KEK slot and converts the key table stored on the HSM to encryption under the new major key.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permissions | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Major Keys:Rotate | Switch the MFK and the Pending-MFK. | Mgmt | 2 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `SMFK` |\n\n<a id=\"optional-bj-operation\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) BJ - Operation\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `0`: Switch Major Key and KEK (default)<br>`1`: Return the key table status only |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-major-key-to-be-rotated-with-kek\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - Major Key to be rotated with KEK\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: MFK (default)<br>`6`: PMK<br>`7`: FTK (if PKCS11 is available) |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `SMFK` |\n\n<a id=\"bb-success-indicator\"></a>\n\n### BB - Success Indicator\n\nReturned only when request token **BJ** is `0`.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Alphabetic | `Y`: Conversion was successful<br>`N`: Conversion was not successful |\n\n<a id=\"fs-key-table-status\"></a>\n\n### FS - Key Table Status\n\nReturned only when request token **BJ** is `1`.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `0`: Key table not locked<br>`1`: Key table locked |\n\n<a id=\"sw-list-all-swappable-slots-with-kek\"></a>\n\n### SW - List all swappable slots with KEK\n\nReturned only when request token **BJ** is `-1`.\n\nReturned empty if nothing can be swapped.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Variable | ASCII | A - Z, a - z, 0 - 9 except ; [ ] |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"switch-the-mfk/kek-and-translate-the-keys\"></a>\n\n### Switch the MFK/KEK and translate the keys\n\n```\nRequest: [AOSMFK;]\n\nResponse: [AOSMFK;BBY;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"status-request-of-the-key-table-not-locked\"></a>\n\n### Status request of the key table (not locked)\n\n```\nRequest: [AOSMFK;BJ1;]\n\nResponse: [AOSMFK;FS0;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"status-request-of-the-key-table-locked\"></a>\n\n### Status request of the key table (locked)\n\n```\nRequest: [AOSMFK;BJ1;]\n\nResponse: [AOSMFK;FS1;]\n```\n"
