      "es": "STCP allows you to view or modify the cipher suites and protocol versions enabled on a given TLS processing pair. Use this command to harden a connection by disabling weak ciphers or legacy protocols, or to query the currently active configuration. Send the WB token to retrieve a full list of all ciphers and protocols available on the device. Use companion command STSI to manage other TLS pair settings such as port numbers, interfaces, and certificate sources.",
