    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# STRS: Restart the TLS Processing Pair Count\n\nFuente: [STRS: Restart the TLS Processing Pair Count](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/system/tls/strs-restart-the-tls-processing-pair-count)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:18:01.037Z\n\n---\n\nSTRS restarts the TLS processor or a specific TLS processing pair on the HSM. This is required because the TLS processor no longer automatically restarts when a change is detected in the SRAM configuration. You can restart all pairs at once by omitting the TP token, or target a single pair by specifying its index.\n\n> **Note:** - Internal pairs cannot be restarted while in FIPS mode unless they are valid. A reboot of the firmware is required in this case.\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| TLS Settings:Modify | Configure the TLS settings for any port. | Mgmt | 2 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `TP` | Pair to restart | Numeric | 1-2 | Optional |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `TY` | Success indicator | Alphabetic | 1 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\nCommand ID for this request.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `STRS` |\n\n<a id=\"optional-tp-pair-to-restart\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) TP - Pair to restart\n\nIndex of the specific TLS processing pair to restart. If not sent, all pairs are restarted.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-2 | Numeric | Pair index to restart |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id-2\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\nEchoes the command code from the request.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `STRS` |\n\n<a id=\"ty-success-indicator\"></a>\n\n### TY - Success indicator\n\nIndicates the TLS processing pair restart succeeded.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Alphabetic | `Y`: Restart completed successfully. |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"restart-a-single-pair\"></a>\n\n### Restart a single pair\n\n```\nRequest: [AOSTRS;TP1;]\n\nResponse: [AOSTRS;TYY;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"restart-all-pairs\"></a>\n\n### Restart all pairs\n\n```\nRequest: [AOSTRS;]\n\nResponse: [AOSTRS;TYY;]\n```\n",
      "en": "# STRS: Restart the TLS Processing Pair Count\n\nFuente: [STRS: Restart the TLS Processing Pair Count](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/system/tls/strs-restart-the-tls-processing-pair-count)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:18:01.037Z\n\n---\n\nSTRS restarts the TLS processor or a specific TLS processing pair on the HSM. This is required because the TLS processor no longer automatically restarts when a change is detected in the SRAM configuration. You can restart all pairs at once by omitting the TP token, or target a single pair by specifying its index.\n\n> **Note:** - Internal pairs cannot be restarted while in FIPS mode unless they are valid. A reboot of the firmware is required in this case.\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| TLS Settings:Modify | Configure the TLS settings for any port. | Mgmt | 2 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `TP` | Pair to restart | Numeric | 1-2 | Optional |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `TY` | Success indicator | Alphabetic | 1 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\nCommand ID for this request.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `STRS` |\n\n<a id=\"optional-tp-pair-to-restart\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) TP - Pair to restart\n\nIndex of the specific TLS processing pair to restart. If not sent, all pairs are restarted.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-2 | Numeric | Pair index to restart |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id-2\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\nEchoes the command code from the request.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `STRS` |\n\n<a id=\"ty-success-indicator\"></a>\n\n### TY - Success indicator\n\nIndicates the TLS processing pair restart succeeded.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Alphabetic | `Y`: Restart completed successfully. |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"restart-a-single-pair\"></a>\n\n### Restart a single pair\n\n```\nRequest: [AOSTRS;TP1;]\n\nResponse: [AOSTRS;TYY;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"restart-all-pairs\"></a>\n\n### Restart all pairs\n\n```\nRequest: [AOSTRS;]\n\nResponse: [AOSTRS;TYY;]\n```\n"
    }
