    "summary": {
      "es": "STSI provides comprehensive control over TLS processing pair configuration. You can set or query port numbers, interfaces, buffer sizes, cipher types, certificate sources, connection limits, and other pair-level settings. Send any optional token with `-1` to return the current value, or `-2` to reset it to the device default. Use companion command STCP to configure specific cipher suites and protocol versions for a pair.\n\n> **Note:** - This command does not allow changes to the internal HTTP or Admin pairs or allow non-SSL connections to HTTP or Admin while in FIPS mode.",
      "en": "STSI provides comprehensive control over TLS processing pair configuration. You can set or query port numbers, interfaces, buffer sizes, cipher types, certificate sources, connection limits, and other pair-level settings. Send any optional token with `-1` to return the current value, or `-2` to reset it to the device default. Use companion command STCP to configure specific cipher suites and protocol versions for a pair.\n\n> **Note:** - This command does not allow changes to the internal HTTP or Admin pairs or allow non-SSL connections to HTTP or Admin while in FIPS mode."
    },
