      "es": "# TCRT: Translate Key from CRT to Futurex Format\n\nFuente: [TCRT: Translate Key from CRT to Futurex Format](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/translate/tcrt-translate-key-from-crt-to-futurex-format)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:09:28.359Z\n\n---\n\nThis command takes in a private key as encrypted CRT components. The components are internally decrypted and translated for encryption under a major key and, optionally, a defined KEK by using the Futurex format for storing private keys.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| RSA | Enables commands requiring RSA functionality. |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `TCRT` |\n\n<a id=\"ak-input-kek-encrypted-under-mod-0-of-the-mfk\"></a>\n\n### AK - Input KEK encrypted under mod 0 of the MFK\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Variable | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"optional-ap-output-kek-encrypted-under-mod-0-of-the-mfk\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) AP - Output KEK encrypted under mod 0 of the MFK\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Variable | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"al-crt-components-encrypted-under-the-input-kek\"></a>\n\n### AL - CRT components encrypted under the input KEK\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2-2048 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"gm-cipher-mode\"></a>\n\n### GM - Cipher Mode\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-2 | Numeric | `0`: ECB<br>`1`: CBC (default)<br>`50`: EDEx |\n\n<a id=\"at-padding-mode\"></a>\n\n### AT - Padding Mode:\n\n**Note** This is ignored when using EDEx cipher.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `0`: No padding<br>`1`: PKCS Standard padding (default)<br>`2`: Bit Padding (0x80 … 0x00) |\n\n<a id=\"optional-only-used-if-cbc-gh-iv-under-modifier-6-of-the-mfk\"></a>\n\n### (Optional, only used if CBC) GH - IV under modifier 6 of the MFK\n\n**Note** If not present, this field defaults to an IV of binary zeros.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Variable | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"gk-translation-mode\"></a>\n\n### GK - Translation Mode\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `0`: p, q,dP, dQ, qInv, Modulus (default)<br>`1`: d, n, e |\n\n<a id=\"ba-dp-offset\"></a>\n\n### BA - dP offset\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"bb-dp-length\"></a>\n\n### BB - dP length\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"bc-dq-offset\"></a>\n\n### BC - dQ offset\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"bd-dq-length\"></a>\n\n### BD - dQ length\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"be-p-offset\"></a>\n\n### BE - p offset\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"bf-p-length\"></a>\n\n### BF - p length\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"bg-q-offset\"></a>\n\n### BG - q offset\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"bh-q-length\"></a>\n\n### BH - q length\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"bi-qinv-offset\"></a>\n\n### BI - qInv offset\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"bj-qinv-length\"></a>\n\n### BJ - qInv length\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"wg-modulus\"></a>\n\n### WG - Modulus\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Variable | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"wf-n\"></a>\n\n### WF - n\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Variable | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"ca-d-offset\"></a>\n\n### CA - d Offset\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"cb-d-length\"></a>\n\n### CB - d length\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-major-key-that-keys-are-under\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - Major Key that keys are under\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: MFK (default)<br>`6`: PMK<br>`7`: FTK (if PKCS11 is available) |\n\n<a id=\"optional-pmk-only-cz-key-usage-constant\"></a>\n\n### (Optional, PMK only) CZ - Key Usage Constant\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Alphanumeric | `B`: Encrypt & Decrypt<br>`E`: Encrypt<br>`D`: Decrypt<br>`C`: Generate & Verify MAC<br>`G`: Generate MAC / Sign-only<br>`V`: Verify MAC / Verify-only<br>`X`: Derive<br>`S`: Asymmetric Sign & Verify (default)<br>`1`: Asymmetric Wrap<br>`2`: Asymmetric Unwrap<br>`3`: Asymmetric Wrap & Unwrap |\n\n<a id=\"optional-pmk-only-sf-security-usage-flags\"></a>\n\n### (Optional, PMK only) SF - Security Usage Flags\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `0`: None<br>`1`: Private<br>`2`: Sensitive<br>`4`: Immutable |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `TCRT` |\n\n<a id=\"rc-private-key\"></a>\n\n### RC - Private key\n\nThis field is a private key encrypted under modifier **0** of the MFK (if no output KEK was provided).\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Variable | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"sd-private-key\"></a>\n\n### SD - Private key\n\nThis field is a private key encrypted under modifier **0** of the KEK (if one was provided).\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Variable | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"xc-check-digits-of-the-output-kek-if-one-was-provided\"></a>\n\n### XC - Check digits of the output KEK (if one was provided)\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4-6 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"ae-check-digits-of-the-private-key\"></a>\n\n### AE - Check digits of the private key\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 8 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"example-1\"></a>\n\n### Example 1\n\n```\nRequest: [AORCRT;;GK4;GM1;]\n\nResponse: [AORCRT;WA128;WB128;WC128;WD128;WE128;;;AE83E0D2E4;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"example-2\"></a>\n\n### Example 2\n\n```\nRequest: [AOTCRT;;BB128;BD128;BF128;BH128;BJ128;BE8;BG136;BA264;BC392;BI520;AT0;;]\n\nResponse: [AOTCRT;;AE83E0D2E4;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"test-key-used\"></a>\n\n### Test Key Used\n\nMFK Test Key: D2DE5CD9110F4CAB 1111111111111111 0123456789ABCDEF Check Digit: (financial 8071) (cmac 9652)\n",
