    "summary": {
      "es": "This command translates and parses data from a key derived using DUKPT to an RSA public key with specific track data.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The encrypted output has the following format: ***KEYIDKEYIDKEYIDDATA***, where *$KEYID* is the last 8 bytes of the Key ID sent by the user (if any).\n- For more information about DUKPT, see ANSI X9.24, Part 1 - Annex A.\n- Both token **FN** (first name) and token **LN** (last name) are found in a single field inside Track 1. This **Name** field is at most 26 characters long, including the separator (if any). The field can contain just the first name or last name. Therefore, the maximum length of both first name and last name can be up to 26 characters.",
      "en": "This command translates and parses data from a key derived using DUKPT to an RSA public key with specific track data.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The encrypted output has the following format: ***KEYIDKEYIDKEYIDDATA***, where *$KEYID* is the last 8 bytes of the Key ID sent by the user (if any).\n- For more information about DUKPT, see ANSI X9.24, Part 1 - Annex A.\n- Both token **FN** (first name) and token **LN** (last name) are found in a single field inside Track 1. This **Name** field is at most 26 characters long, including the separator (if any). The field can contain just the first name or last name. Therefore, the maximum length of both first name and last name can be up to 26 characters."
    },
