      "es": "This command is used to translate PIN blocks from one key to another key.\n\nThis command performs an edit test to verify that the incoming PIN block follows the rules for the specified type of PIN block (specified in token **AW**). If the PIN block fails, Excrypt performs the translation but returns a PIN format error.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in PCI HSM mode when Clear PIN license is enabled.\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- There are three different request variations for the TPIN command that are included in this document:  \n\n  - **TPIN**: Translates PIN blocks from one key to another key.\n  - **TPIN IBM**: Decrypts the incoming PIN block encrypted via the IBM 4736 ATM algorithm under one key and re-encrypts the PIN block under another key.\n  - **TPIN DUKPT**: Enables the incoming DUKPT encrypted PIN block to be decrypted and then re-encrypted (translated) under an outgoing key.",
