      "es": "# TWKB: Translate Key From AKB to ECB/CBC DES\n\nFuente: [TWKB: Translate Key From AKB to ECB/CBC DES](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/translate/twkb-translate-key-from-akb-to-ecbcbc-des)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:10:15.701Z\n\n---\n\nThis command takes a working key encrypted under the key encryption key (KEK) in AKB format and convert it to a cryptogram in DES format (still encrypted under the KEK).\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- You can specify the command mode for CBC DES or EBC DES.\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `TWKB` |\n\n<a id=\"as-modifier-of-the-kek-to-be-used-for-encryption\"></a>\n\n### AS - Modifier of the KEK to be used for encryption\n\nSee **Key modifiers** resource for the full list.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-2 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"ap-kek-encrypted-under-mfk-in-akb-format\"></a>\n\n### AP - KEK encrypted under MFK in AKB format\n\n**Note** This has to be a KEK with both encrypt and decrypt usages (‘N’).\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 74 | ASCII | A-Z, a-z, 0-9 except ; [ ] |\n\n<a id=\"bg-working-key-in-akb-format\"></a>\n\n### BG - Working key in AKB format\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 74 | ASCII | A-Z, a-z, 0-9 except ; [ ] |\n\n<a id=\"optional-fs-mode-for-des-decryption\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) FS - Mode for DES decryption\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: CBC (default)<br>`2`: ECB |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `TWKB` |\n\n<a id=\"bh-working-key-encrypted-under-variant/modifier-of-kek-in-des-format\"></a>\n\n### BH - Working key encrypted under variant/modifier of KEK in DES format\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 48 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"ae-check-digit-of-the-working-key\"></a>\n\n### AE - Check digit of the working key\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command Examples\n\n<a id=\"using-default-cbc-des-encryption\"></a>\n\n## Using default CBC DES encryption\n\n```\nRequest: [AOTWKB;AS0;AP1KDNE000,8F9673916A106BB8A77A523C961F94C7F7BCAD54E1550671,7113B1EBBCE811FF;BG1PUNE000,F19AB270BD66314BC04A30A9C1C81AB0787854EB0A044DEA,5801B818688303F2;]\n\nResponse: [AOTWKB;BH1FD1B02B237AF9AE3702240E7080EA4C;AE7B83;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"using-ecb-des-encryption\"></a>\n\n## Using ECB DES encryption\n\n```\nRequest: [AOTWKB;AS0;AP1KDNE000,8F9673916A106BB8A77A523C961F94C7F7BCAD54E1550671,7113B1EBBCE811FF;BG1PUNE000,F19AB270BD66314BC04A30A9C1C81AB0787854EB0A044DEA,5801B818688303F2;FS2;]\n\nResponse: [AOTWKB;BH1FD1B02B237AF9AE1A4D672DCA6CB335;AE7B83;]\n```\n",
