      "en": "This command translates the incoming key from encryption under the key encryption key (KEK) to encryption under the local HSM Major Key.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The HSM receiving an encrypted working key from another HSM typically uses this function.\n- Although you can place tokens in most Excrypt API commands in any order, for **TWKL**, token **AS** must precede token **BH** to enable Excrypt to know what modifier to use before translating the key.\n- We provided **TWKL** for historical compatibility with other security devices. Installations using more than one KEK likely prefer command **TWKS**, which provides the same functionality as **TWKL** but also allows specification of a KEK key block or cryptogram."
