    "name": {
      "es": "VAAV: Verify Account Holder Authentication Value",
      "en": "VAAV: Verify Account Holder Authentication Value"
    },
    "summary": {
      "es": "This command verifies that the Account Holder Authentication Value (AAV) given is the correct AAV according to the data held about the account when using Mastercard’s implementation of 3-D Secure or a CVV2 when using the Visa CAAV V7 PA method.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- In Firmware version 7.6.1.23 and later CVC/CVV AKB headers 1CD**000 can be used regardless of how the *Use Compatibility Modifier For CVC/CVV Generation/Verification* setting is set.",
      "en": "This command verifies that the Account Holder Authentication Value (AAV) given is the correct AAV according to the data held about the account when using Mastercard’s implementation of 3-D Secure or a CVV2 when using the Visa CAAV V7 PA method.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- In Firmware version 7.6.1.23 and later CVC/CVV AKB headers 1CD**000 can be used regardless of how the *Use Compatibility Modifier For CVC/CVV Generation/Verification* setting is set."
    },
    "description": {
      "es": "This command verifies that the Account Holder Authentication Value (AAV) given is the correct AAV according to the data held about the account when using Mastercard’s implementation of 3-D Secure or a CVV2 when using the Visa CAAV V7 PA method.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- In Firmware version 7.6.1.23 and later CVC/CVV AKB headers 1CD**000 can be used regardless of how the *Use Compatibility Modifier For CVC/CVV Generation/Verification* setting is set.",
      "en": "This command verifies that the Account Holder Authentication Value (AAV) given is the correct AAV according to the data held about the account when using Mastercard’s implementation of 3-D Secure or a CVV2 when using the Visa CAAV V7 PA method.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- In Firmware version 7.6.1.23 and later CVC/CVV AKB headers 1CD**000 can be used regardless of how the *Use Compatibility Modifier For CVC/CVV Generation/Verification* setting is set."
    },
