      "es": "This command verifies a Mastercard Card Verification Code (CVC), Card Verification Code 2 (CVC2), or both.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- Mastercard uses the CVC and CVC2 as a checksum for transaction authentication. The CVC code is encoded on the card’s magnetic stripe. The CVC2 code is the embossed value on the front of the card.\n- The cryptogram is encrypted under a different modifier when using CVC Compatibility Mode. For more information, see the **CVC compatibility code** resource.",
      "en": "This command verifies a Mastercard Card Verification Code (CVC), Card Verification Code 2 (CVC2), or both.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- Mastercard uses the CVC and CVC2 as a checksum for transaction authentication. The CVC code is encoded on the card’s magnetic stripe. The CVC2 code is the embossed value on the front of the card.\n- The cryptogram is encrypted under a different modifier when using CVC Compatibility Mode. For more information, see the **CVC compatibility code** resource."
