    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# VKBL: Verify AKB key block\n\nFuente: [VKBL: Verify AKB key block](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/validate/vkbl-verify-key-block)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:11:10.616Z\n\n---\n\nThis command takes an AKB format key block and verifies its integrity by comparing the check digits in the message authentication code (MAC) against those the command generates on its own.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- You must enable the option to use AKB on the HSM.\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `AS` | Modifier | Numeric | 1 | Yes |\n| `KB` | AKB format key block | ASCII | 74 | Yes |\n| `AP` | Key Encryption Key | <br><br>Hexadecimal<br><br>ASCII<br><br>Alphanumeric<br><br> | <br><br>16, 32, 48<br><br>74, 88+<br><br>3-7<br><br> | Optional |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `BB` | Response code | Alphabetic | 1 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `VKBL` |\n\n<a id=\"as-modifier\"></a>\n\n### AS - Modifier\n\nSee **Key modifiers** resource for full list.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"kb-akb-format-key-block\"></a>\n\n### KB - AKB format key block\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 74 | ASCII | A-Z, a-z, 0-9 except ; [ ] |\n\n<a id=\"optional-ap-key-encryption-key\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) AP - Key Encryption Key\n\nIf not sent, the MFK is used in place of the KEK.\n\nThis field supports the following formats:\n\n- Cryptogram\n- Key block\n- Key Storage Table index\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16<br>32<br>48 | Hexadecimal | **Cryptogram**<br>0-9, A-F |\n| 74<br>88+ | ASCII | **Key block**<br>A - Z, a - z, 0 - 9 except ; [ ] |\n| 3-7 | Alphanumeric | BD + key slot number |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `VKBL` |\n\n<a id=\"bb-response-code\"></a>\n\n### BB - Response code\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Alphabetic | `Y`: Verified<br>`N`: Not Verified |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"verified\"></a>\n\n## Verified\n\n```\nRequest: [AOVKBL;AS1;KB1KDNE000,619DCE86A08691080C476C703BBE511829E7EDFA50D178BC,596259E8A040BF92;]\n\nResponse: [AOVKBL;BBY;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"not-verified\"></a>\n\n## Not verified\n\n```\nRequest: [AOVKBL;AS1;KB1KDNE000,619DCE86A08691080C476C703BBE511829E7EDFA50D178BC,596259E8A040BF92;APD2DE5CD9110F4CAB11111111111111110123456789ABCDEF;]\n\nResponse: [AOVKBL;BBN;]\n```\n",
      "en": "# VKBL: Verify AKB key block\n\nFuente: [VKBL: Verify AKB key block](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/validate/vkbl-verify-key-block)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:11:10.616Z\n\n---\n\nThis command takes an AKB format key block and verifies its integrity by comparing the check digits in the message authentication code (MAC) against those the command generates on its own.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- You must enable the option to use AKB on the HSM.\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `AS` | Modifier | Numeric | 1 | Yes |\n| `KB` | AKB format key block | ASCII | 74 | Yes |\n| `AP` | Key Encryption Key | <br><br>Hexadecimal<br><br>ASCII<br><br>Alphanumeric<br><br> | <br><br>16, 32, 48<br><br>74, 88+<br><br>3-7<br><br> | Optional |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `BB` | Response code | Alphabetic | 1 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `VKBL` |\n\n<a id=\"as-modifier\"></a>\n\n### AS - Modifier\n\nSee **Key modifiers** resource for full list.\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"kb-akb-format-key-block\"></a>\n\n### KB - AKB format key block\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 74 | ASCII | A-Z, a-z, 0-9 except ; [ ] |\n\n<a id=\"optional-ap-key-encryption-key\"></a>\n\n### (Optional) AP - Key Encryption Key\n\nIf not sent, the MFK is used in place of the KEK.\n\nThis field supports the following formats:\n\n- Cryptogram\n- Key block\n- Key Storage Table index\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 16<br>32<br>48 | Hexadecimal | **Cryptogram**<br>0-9, A-F |\n| 74<br>88+ | ASCII | **Key block**<br>A - Z, a - z, 0 - 9 except ; [ ] |\n| 3-7 | Alphanumeric | BD + key slot number |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `VKBL` |\n\n<a id=\"bb-response-code\"></a>\n\n### BB - Response code\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Alphabetic | `Y`: Verified<br>`N`: Not Verified |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"verified\"></a>\n\n## Verified\n\n```\nRequest: [AOVKBL;AS1;KB1KDNE000,619DCE86A08691080C476C703BBE511829E7EDFA50D178BC,596259E8A040BF92;]\n\nResponse: [AOVKBL;BBY;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"not-verified\"></a>\n\n## Not verified\n\n```\nRequest: [AOVKBL;AS1;KB1KDNE000,619DCE86A08691080C476C703BBE511829E7EDFA50D178BC,596259E8A040BF92;APD2DE5CD9110F4CAB11111111111111110123456789ABCDEF;]\n\nResponse: [AOVKBL;BBN;]\n```\n"
    }
