    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# VKTE: Verify Key Table Entry\n\nFuente: [VKTE: Verify Key Table Entry](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/key_tables/vkte-verify-key-table-entry)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:11:12.075Z\n\n---\n\nThis command verifies a key table entry by displaying the checksum for a specified slot.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- You can also use this command to verify whether a table slot is empty or filled.\n- References to index location are in decimal notation.\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| Financial Processing | Enabled by default on all Excrypt Series HSMs and as an add-on license for Vectera Series HSMs. |\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required Permissions\n\n| Permissions | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Keys | View key and table information | Mgmt | 0 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `BD` | Table Index to verify | Numeric | 1-4 | Yes |\n| `AS` | Modifier to use | Numeric | 1 | Yes |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `BD` | Table Index location verified | Numeric | 1-4 |\n| `BQ` | Number of available entries | Numeric | 1-4 |\n| `AE` | Check digit of the key position being verified | Hexadecimal | 1-8 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `VKTE` |\n\n<a id=\"bd-table-index-to-verify\"></a>\n\n### BD - Table Index to verify\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | 0 - 3999 |\n\nAS - Modifier to use\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `0`: Key Exchange Key (KEK)<br>`1`: PIN Encryption Key (PEK)<br>`2`: Data Encryption Key (DEK)<br>`3`: Message Authentication Key (MAK)<br>`4`: PIN Verification Key (PVK)<br>`5`: ATM Key<br>`9`: PIN Generation Key (PGK) |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `VKTE` |\n\n<a id=\"bd-table-index-location-verified\"></a>\n\n### BD - Table Index location verified\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | 0 - 3999 |\n\n<a id=\"bq-number-of-available-entries\"></a>\n\n### BQ - Number of available entries\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | 0 - 9 |\n\n<a id=\"ae-check-digit-of-the-key-position-being-verified\"></a>\n\n### AE - Check digit of the key position being verified\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-8 | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n```\nRequest: [AOVKTE;BD123;AS1;]\n\nResponse: [AOVKTE;BD123;BQ3862;AE059A;]\n```\n",
      "en": "# VKTE: Verify Key Table Entry\n\nFuente: [VKTE: Verify Key Table Entry](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/key_tables/vkte-verify-key-table-entry)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:11:12.075Z\n\n---\n\nThis command verifies a key table entry by displaying the checksum for a specified slot.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n> **Danger:** Disabled in FIPS Mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- You can also use this command to verify whether a table slot is empty or filled.\n- References to index location are in decimal notation.\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| Financial Processing | Enabled by default on all Excrypt Series HSMs and as an add-on license for Vectera Series HSMs. |\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required Permissions\n\n| Permissions | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Keys | View key and table information | Mgmt | 0 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command ID | Alphabetic | 4 | Yes |\n| `BD` | Table Index to verify | Numeric | 1-4 | Yes |\n| `AS` | Modifier to use | Numeric | 1 | Yes |\n\nResponse tokens\n\n| Token | Parameter | Type | Length |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AO` | Command Response ID | Alphabetic | 4 |\n| `BD` | Table Index location verified | Numeric | 1-4 |\n| `BQ` | Number of available entries | Numeric | 1-4 |\n| `AE` | Check digit of the key position being verified | Hexadecimal | 1-8 |\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `VKTE` |\n\n<a id=\"bd-table-index-to-verify\"></a>\n\n### BD - Table Index to verify\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | 0 - 3999 |\n\nAS - Modifier to use\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `0`: Key Exchange Key (KEK)<br>`1`: PIN Encryption Key (PEK)<br>`2`: Data Encryption Key (DEK)<br>`3`: Message Authentication Key (MAK)<br>`4`: PIN Verification Key (PVK)<br>`5`: ATM Key<br>`9`: PIN Generation Key (PGK) |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `VKTE` |\n\n<a id=\"bd-table-index-location-verified\"></a>\n\n### BD - Table Index location verified\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | 0 - 3999 |\n\n<a id=\"bq-number-of-available-entries\"></a>\n\n### BQ - Number of available entries\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-4 | Numeric | 0 - 9 |\n\n<a id=\"ae-check-digit-of-the-key-position-being-verified\"></a>\n\n### AE - Check digit of the key position being verified\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-8 | Hexadecimal | 0 - 9, A - F |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n```\nRequest: [AOVKTE;BD123;AS1;]\n\nResponse: [AOVKTE;BD123;BQ3862;AE059A;]\n```\n"
    }
