    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# VRSA: Verify RSA Key Table Entry\n\nFuente: [VRSA: Verify RSA Key Table Entry](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/validate/vrsa-verify-rsa-key-table-entry)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:11:48.054Z\n\n---\n\nThis command verifies an RSA key index and outputs information about the key at that index.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The **Key slot offset** differs between the API and Excrypt. While the API recognizes PKI storage to be slots 0-99, the Excrypt Manager loads keys into slots 1-100. Therefore, for tokens that support PKI storage table indexing, the key slot in which the key is loaded using Excrypt Manager is off by one. For example, a key loaded into slot** 1** on the Excrypt Manager is referenced in the API slot **0**.\n- If the key index has no key, response tokens **BB** and **BQ** are empty, and **RB** is not returned.\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| RSA | Enables commands requiring RSA functionality. |\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Keys | View key and table information | Mgmt | 0 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `VRSA` |\n\n<a id=\"rd-index-of-the-key-that-is-being-verified\"></a>\n\n### RD - Index of the key that is being verified\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-2 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `VRSA` |\n\n<a id=\"ae-check-digit-of-the-key\"></a>\n\n### AE - Check digit of the key\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 8 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"bb-type-of-key\"></a>\n\n### BB - Type of key\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: Private Key 2: Public Key |\n\n<a id=\"bq-number-of-remaining-key-slots-available\"></a>\n\n### BQ - Number of remaining key slots available\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-2 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"rb-bit-size-of-the-rsa-key\"></a>\n\n### RB - Bit size of the RSA key\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 3-4 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"key-in-pki-key-slot-0-excrypt-manager-slot-1\"></a>\n\n### Key in PKI Key Slot 0, Excrypt Manager Slot 1\n\n```\nRequest: [AOVRSA;RD0;]\n\nResponse: [AOVRSA;AEDDB7F807;BB1;BQ94;RB2048;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"no-key-in-pki-key-slot-55-excrypt-manager-slot-56\"></a>\n\n### **No Key in PKI Key Slot 55, Excrypt Manager Slot 56**\n\n```\nRequest: [AOVRSA;RD55;]\n\nResponse: [AOVRSA;AE;BB;BQ94;RB1400;]\n```\n",
      "en": "# VRSA: Verify RSA Key Table Entry\n\nFuente: [VRSA: Verify RSA Key Table Entry](https://docs.futurex.com/HSM_Commands/7.6.1.x/Excrypt_commands/keys/validate/vrsa-verify-rsa-key-table-entry)  \nVersión del catálogo: **7.6.1.x**  \nCapturado: 2026-10-01T08:11:48.054Z\n\n---\n\nThis command verifies an RSA key index and outputs information about the key at that index.\n\n> **Check:** Enabled in PCI HSM mode\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The **Key slot offset** differs between the API and Excrypt. While the API recognizes PKI storage to be slots 0-99, the Excrypt Manager loads keys into slots 1-100. Therefore, for tokens that support PKI storage table indexing, the key slot in which the key is loaded using Excrypt Manager is off by one. For example, a key loaded into slot** 1** on the Excrypt Manager is referenced in the API slot **0**.\n- If the key index has no key, response tokens **BB** and **BQ** are empty, and **RB** is not returned.\n\n<a id=\"required-licenses\"></a>\n\n## Required licenses\n\n| License Name | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| RSA | Enables commands requiring RSA functionality. |\n\n<a id=\"required-permissions\"></a>\n\n## Required permissions\n\n| Permission | Description | Port | Min Logins |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Keys | View key and table information | Mgmt | 0 |\n\n<a id=\"token-summary\"></a>\n\n## Token summary\n\nAt-a-glance request and response tokens for this command. For accepted values, conditional rules, and usage notes, see the detailed token sections below.\n\nRequest tokens\n\nResponse tokens\n\n<a id=\"request-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Request tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `VRSA` |\n\n<a id=\"rd-index-of-the-key-that-is-being-verified\"></a>\n\n### RD - Index of the key that is being verified\n\n| Length | Data Type | Accepted Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-2 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"response-tokens\"></a>\n\n## Response tokens\n\n<a id=\"ao-command-response-id\"></a>\n\n### AO - Command Response ID\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 4 | Alphabetic | `VRSA` |\n\n<a id=\"ae-check-digit-of-the-key\"></a>\n\n### AE - Check digit of the key\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 8 | Hexadecimal | 0-9, A-F |\n\n<a id=\"bb-type-of-key\"></a>\n\n### BB - Type of key\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Numeric | `1`: Private Key 2: Public Key |\n\n<a id=\"bq-number-of-remaining-key-slots-available\"></a>\n\n### BQ - Number of remaining key slots available\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1-2 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"rb-bit-size-of-the-rsa-key\"></a>\n\n### RB - Bit size of the RSA key\n\n| Length | Data Type | Returned Values |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 3-4 | Numeric | 0-9 |\n\n<a id=\"command-examples\"></a>\n\n## Command examples\n\n<a id=\"key-in-pki-key-slot-0-excrypt-manager-slot-1\"></a>\n\n### Key in PKI Key Slot 0, Excrypt Manager Slot 1\n\n```\nRequest: [AOVRSA;RD0;]\n\nResponse: [AOVRSA;AEDDB7F807;BB1;BQ94;RB2048;]\n```\n\n<a id=\"no-key-in-pki-key-slot-55-excrypt-manager-slot-56\"></a>\n\n### **No Key in PKI Key Slot 55, Excrypt Manager Slot 56**\n\n```\nRequest: [AOVRSA;RD55;]\n\nResponse: [AOVRSA;AE;BB;BQ94;RB1400;]\n```\n"
    }
